(Phnom Penh): As the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia is ready to host the 45th ASEAN-EU Summit to be held in Brussels, Belgium in 2022. This was stated by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia in the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with the European Union, which was held on August 6, 2021 via video.
To mark the 45th anniversary of ASEAN-EU relations, the ASEAN Foreign Ministers supported the EU's request to organize the event, according to a press release obtained by Fresh News on 7 August 2021. 2022 Anniversary Summit in Brussels
"Cambodia, as chair of ASEAN in 2022, is ready to work with the Philippines, the next ASEAN-EU facilitator, with other ASEAN member states and "The European Union to ensure the success of the ASEAN-EU Summit in 2022."
The Meeting welcomed the promotion of ASEAN-EU relations to a strategic partnership as agreed at the 23rd ASEAN-EU Foreign Ministers' Meeting on December 1, 2020 and expressed satisfaction with Achievements and Progress Achieved in the Implementation of the ASEAN-EU Action Plan (2018-2022).
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers commended the EU's commitment to the ASEAN Middle East and its ASEAN-led mechanisms based on common beliefs in a multilateral order based on the rule of law, especially when dealing with regional and international issues. Common concern.
He also stressed the importance of further joint efforts to strengthen ASEAN-EU economic cooperation and the multilateral trading system based on legal principles, including through the achievement of Potential of the ASEAN-EU Free Trade Agreement (ASEAN-EU FTA).
