The Prime Minister's expression of pride was expressed through his congratulatory message on the occasion of ASEAN Day, August 8, 2021.
"On this auspicious occasion for all ASEAN people as we celebrate the 54th anniversary of the establishment of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) with pride," he said. "We have all come a long way and have made remarkable progress in aiming to move this regional organization into a cohesive entity and a larger population." .
Over the past five decades, ASEAN has expanded its membership to include all but one country in the region and promoted political, economic and social integration among its member countries and partners. ASEAN has also strengthened its prestige as one of the most dynamic and vibrant regional organizations in the world in terms of economic potential and comparative benefits.
This year, Brunei, the rotating chair of ASEAN, is committed to further moving the ASEAN process forward under the theme "We care, we are ready, we grow", which best fits with the acute geopolitical and Current socio-economics to achieve the ASEAN Community Vision 2025.
According to Samdech Techo, the Supreme Leader of the Royal Government of Cambodia, based on this reason, ASEAN has always been an important and inseparable part of Cambodia's foreign policy. Through the ASEAN framework, we are able to maximize opportunities to enhance friendly relations and cooperation with countries in the region and external partners around the world in the cause of promoting lasting peace, security, prosperity and national development in all aspects.
