Tbong Khmum provincial authorities continue to tighten border checkpoints as instructed by the Royal Government, but traffic is still normal
(Tbong Khmum): After the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Royal Government decided to close all border crossings with Vietnam, especially Tbong Khmum, which is a border province with 7 border crossings, the provincial administration has continued to tighten. The people of the two countries are strictly not allowed to cross, while only the normal exchange of goods is allowed at zero.
Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, said that the provincial authorities have placed strict security guards at all border crossings, including corridors, to prevent people from crossing the border between the two countries, but the exchange of goods is still Normal.
According to Mr. Phan Kimson, Director of Trapeang Phlong International Border Gate in Ponhea Krek District, today, for the movement of goods, it is still common practice in both Cambodia and Vietnam to change the driver and the head of the vehicle at zero with no alcohol spray. Exchange.
He said that after the order of the Royal Government as well as the provincial administration, the competent officials were deployed 24 hours to guard, in which the Vietnamese also deployed the same resistance force.
Similarly, Mr. Muon Sopheap, head of the bilateral border checkpoint in Memot district, said that after the order of the Royal Government as well as the provincial administration, the authorities have deployed 24 hours to guard the border smuggling. Of the people of both countries to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
