Japan is a country that has made many contributions to the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against the Kovid 19 epidemic. During the delivery and receiving of the vaccine on July 23, the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, Mikami Masahiro, stated that the provision of 1 million doses of vaccine was in line with the Japan-Cambodia relationship and based on the Kovid situation. 19 in Cambodia today.
The Ambassador expressed hope that the vaccine would support the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to combat Kovid 19 as well as alleviate some of the concerns of the Cambodian people.
According to the Ambassador to Cambodia, the Japanese government has so far provided more than $ 50 million in assistance to Cambodia. These include the provision of medical facilities, hospital improvements, support for international organizations' projects for measures to prevent cross-border transmission, as well as the provision of proper transport and storage of vaccines.
In addition, the Japanese government has provided about $ 227 million in loans to be used in cash aid programs for people affected by Kovid 19 and to strengthen the health system.
The Ambassador also expressed the strong position of the Japanese government in participating in the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia. The Ambassador emphasized that in the fight against Kovid 19, which is a global issue, Japan will continue to cooperate and work with Cambodia, an important friend.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, said in his reception that the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia have warmly welcomed and expressed deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Japan for its support and assistance to Cambodia in the fight against the cause. The epidemic will continue through the provision of aids, medical equipment and financing in the past.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the provision of 1 million doses of vaccine by the Government and people of Japan is a new testimony that reflects the gesture of kindness, kindness and high responsibility of Japan to support the country. Resources and possibilities are limited in the battle against Kovid-19.
