South African authorities say Zuma has been taken to a hospital for medical check-ups after his former health department obtained permission from prison officials to facilitate the necessary proceedings. South African prison officials also stressed that inmates have the right to medical treatment, proper nutrition, reading information and monitoring the conditions of detention.
Former South African President Jacob Zuma was sentenced to 15 months in prison in late June 2021. The sentencing comes after the Constitutional Court found that Jacob Zuma was guilty of defamation of the Constitutional Court's ruling in questioning corruption during his presidency. .
Jacob Zuma's tenure came to an end in 2018 and he has since faced charges of corruption and money laundering, but the former South African president has denied any wrongdoing. He also claimed that he had not committed any crime.
