Last Sunday, Kim Jong Un's half-sister, Kim Yoo-jong, warned that the joint military exercise could damage the two Koreas' relationship and that it was up to South Korea to decide. North Korea has often condemned joint US-South Korean military exercises as a preparation for the overthrow of Kim Jong Un's regime, and Pyongyang routinely launches missile tests in response.
Kim Jong Un is "at least reducing the size of annual military exercises" to test whether North Korea really wants to return to talks.
