Cambodia again requests the Thai side to provide documents on the project to build a stone temple in Borei Ram province, copying the architecture of Angkor Wat
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Culture and Fine Arts of Cambodia has once again requested the Thai side to provide official information and documents on the project to build a stone temple in Borei Ram province that mimics the architecture of Cambodia's Angkor Wat temples.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts on social media, on that occasion, the discussion also raised the case of information on the project to build a stone temple in Borei Ram province, which social media and the media reported that there was a copy. According to the architecture of Angkor Wat. The news was met with outrage from both countries.
In this regard, the Minister requested the Thai side to cooperate in providing specific information and official documents on the project of the construction of the stone temple in Borei Ram province, so that the Cambodian side has a basis to review the implementation of the rules. "Avoid any negative effects that may occur and affect the relationship between the two countries." This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Culture.
The project to build a stone temple in Borei Ram province has received strong reactions from social media users in Cambodia due to its resemblance to the Khmer temple of Angkor Wat.
In early July, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts issued a press release after gathering information related to the construction of a stone temple in Borei Rom, Thailand, similar to Angkor Wat. In a statement from the ministry, the Thai side stated that the construction of the temple did not copy the design or build in the same architectural style as Angkor Wat or any other ancient temple in Cambodia.
