(Phnom Penh): Tea is a drink that can help health, feel fresh and fragrant. But it is believed to have been discovered in 2737 BC by the Chinese emperor Xinong. To date, tea has become the most popular beverage after pure water in the world.
According to research, tea contains antioxidants, minerals, vitamins and calcium. All of these substances are very beneficial to health. But it also contains 40 mg of caffeine, while a cup of fresh coffee contains 85 mg of caffeine.
In China, areas where high consumption of green tea, such as drinking water, has been found to reduce cancer rates by about 60 percent. This is said to be due to the fact that greens have a higher percentage of antioxidants than black tea or other types of tea, which reduce the risk of heart disease.
Tea is now widely used in skin care products to get rid of cancer and wrinkles. Polyphenols found in tea are stronger than any other antioxidant. Consumption of black tea, green tea, yellow tea, oolong tea and fluoride has been found to prevent the formation of plaque and kill bacteria that infect teeth.
