Readers and viewers may wonder why the birth name is "Nal" and why the current Cambodian leader is named "Sen". The name of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was changed during his military service to hide his identity from the enemy.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen were married by the Khmer Rouge on Monday, January 5, 1976 with 12 other couples. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are the 13th couple.
The wedding in the black shirt regime was arranged in the most beautiful way, no traditional costumes, no music, no relatives, no friends to celebrate. The 13 couples were arranged to sit at the table, with the woman sitting in the front and the man in the back. Marriages are announced by a presidency and a committee.
Although the wedding was held in a beautiful atmosphere, the love that was buried deep in the heart made the marriage immortal to this day. Unlike some couples who were forced to marry and forced to marry by the Khmer Rouge, they were forced to part ways when the regime collapsed on January 7, 1979.
The story of love and family life during the Cambodian national era has the legacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. How many other Khmers?
Now, let's get acquainted with the background and life story of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and turn our attention to the history of the struggle for national liberation, the search for peace, the end of the war, the leadership and the efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to develop Cambodia. Named Cambodia's strongest man in the last 40 years or so.
While serving as a resistance soldier in the jungle, due to his intelligence, Comrade Hun Samrech gained the trust of the leadership of the resistance army and evolved from a small soldier to a popular commander. On the battlefield, Commander Hun Samrech, along with other armed fighters, fought side by side with the US and Lon Nol forces of the Khmer Republic.
Victory April 17, 1975 was a joy for the army, but for the fighters, Hun Samrech was not happy with this victory, because he was injured in one eye. The injuries before the victory day of the army until the blindness of Hun Samrech seemed to be a bad omen for all the forest fighters and the Cambodian people as a whole.
The movement to liberate Phnom Penh under the banner of Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk on April 17 was a happy time for the people as well as for the fighters that the war in Cambodia would end and be replaced by peace. It was the desire of the Cambodian people at that time. On the contrary, this victory day turned into a nightmare for some people and leaders of the resistance movement.
After seizing control of Phnom Penh, the top leaders of the Khmer Rouge regime, such as Pol Pot, Nuon Chea, Khieu Samphan, and Ieng Sary, plotted to seize power by killing some resistance leaders and arresting Norodom Sihanouk and his family. Commune in the Royal Palace forces people to leave their homes and work as hard as they can.
Suspicion and fear of losing power forced the leaders of the Democratic Kampuchea regime to massacre many activists, cadres and Cambodians on charges of treason. Under the leadership of Pol Pot and his cronies for three years, eight months and 20 days, more than 2 million Cambodians were killed and died of disease, overwork, and starvation.
Unable to bear the torture and massacre of the Cambodian people, Comrade Hun Sen and four other comrades decided to flee to Vietnam on June 20, 1977 in order to seek the support of Vietnam to overthrow the Khmer Rouge regime.
Leaving his homeland, both risky and risky, to liberate the country and its people from the killing fields at that time was the most difficult and sad time for Comrade Hun Sen compared to the need to leave. Far from home to seek education from childhood in 1965.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once stated that leaving the country at that time did not know whether life came back to his beloved wife and unborn child, who was only 5 months old or not? However, crossing the border at that time had to risk one's life to walk through the minefields listed along the Cambodian-Vietnamese border. Vietnam could be imprisoned or sent back to Pol Pot's government, which is life-threatening.
Under the banner of the "United Front for National Salvation" and the assistance of the Vietnamese army, the Khmer resistance forces led by Comrade Chea Si, Comrade Heng Samrin and Comrade Hun Sen fought hard to overthrow Pol Pot's Democratic Kampuchea regime until victory and victory. Occupied Phnom Penh on January 7, 1979.
Victory on January 7 is a historic victory, a happy time for the Cambodian people, whose lives were rescued from the pit of death. Khmer people who always pray to the gods to save their lives from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot compared January 7, 1979 as their second birthday.
After the liberation, a new regime, the People's Republic of Kampuchea, was established, led by elites, the National Salvation Front. On January 8, Comrade Heng Samrin was appointed Chairman of the Cambodian People's Revolutionary Council, Comrade Pen Sovann as Vice President and Minister of National Defense. Comrade Hun Sen was elected Foreign Minister at the age of 27, the youngest minister in the world.
As the Minister of Foreign Affairs, who has never had the expertise to do this, it is a difficult thing for Comrade Hun Sen. Samdech Techo Hun Sen used to remind that he accepted this role reluctantly because he did not have the skills and experience in this work, but because the will of the young people motivated Samdech to complete the work successfully and proudly.
After serving as Minister of Foreign Affairs, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs for about 6 years, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was elected by the National Assembly of the People's Republic of Cambodia as the Chairman of the Council of Ministers or Prime Minister on the 14th. January 1985 Replaces Chan Si, who died of leukemia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once reminded that Samdech could not accept this position without the support of the party and state leaders, especially Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim, Mr. Say Phu Thong and Mr. Chea Soth. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that Samdech was very surprised at that time, Samdech received 100% of the votes, no opposition ballots, no abstentions and no invalid ballots.
After taking office, not only did he face food shortages, but he also faced many other challenges. The four priority priorities set by the 33-year-old prime minister as his political line are rehabilitation, infrastructure, water, railways and human resource training. The genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
In addition to thinking about rebuilding the country, the Prime Minister of the People's Republic of Kampuchea faced a misunderstanding of the market economy within the party ranks as the remaining Cambodians along the border and other resistance movements took action. Raids and other activities attempt to take over the country again.
In addition, the West not only imposed economic sanctions on the government of Comrade Hun Sen, they also did not recognize the government of the People's Republic of Kampuchea at the United Nations and recognized the Khmer Rouge seat. Despite the complexities and pitfalls, due to the strong unity of the Government of the People's Republic of Cambodia, this issue has been successfully resolved.
In 1986, due to increased workload, Comrade Hun Sen resigned as Minister of Foreign Affairs, transferring to Comrade Kong Koam to have enough time to serve as Chairman of the Council of Ministers or Prime Minister.
Seeing that being in a state of peace and war could not enable Cambodia to develop and bring happiness to its people, and was a threat to its regime. Comrade Hun Sen also wanted to find peace by uniting all parties to the conflict.
In 1987, after a series of peace talks between the government of the People's Republic of Cambodia and the tripartite movement, Comrade Hun Sen took over the post of Foreign Minister to facilitate talks with the leaders of the tripartite movement. Samdech Norodom Sihanouk was the president.
At one point, as soon as he got off the plane, Comrade Hun Sen pulled out a pistol and fired to vent his anger. The shooting was also caused by an angry comrade who did not repair the air conditioner in the office and was emotionally strained after some of the vehicles from the negotiations with the opposition did not get the desired results, while some cadres in The Cambodian People's Revolutionary Party expressed dissatisfaction with the result.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has reminded that there are three most dangerous pressure forces that can affect political life and can affect lives during the negotiations. The three forces include:
In line with the political context, Comrade Hun Sen's Member of Parliament of the People's Republic of Kampuchea changed his name to "State of Cambodia" at the National Assembly session on April 29-30, 1989.
After the Paris Peace Accords, things went according to plan, and Comrade Hun Sen finally returned to Cambodia from Beijing, China, on November 14 from Norodom Sihanouk. 1991. This was his first return after leaving Cambodia on the afternoon of January 6, 1979, before the United Front for the Salvation Army took control of Phnom Penh.
The retirement of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk was warmly welcomed by Comrade Hun Sen and Cambodian government officials. On the streets from the airport to the Royal Palace, students and residents, young and old, men and women, lined up on both sides of the road. Comrade Hun Sen and Samdech Norodom Sihanouk sat and rode in the same car, standing side by side, raising their hands and waving happily to the people on the crowded streets.
The achievement of the Paris Peace Agreement and the return of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk to the motherland of Cambodia is a great development in Cambodian politics and the desire of the Cambodian people who are hungry for the light of peace. Peace, too. But it has not yet reached the end of the dark era of Cambodia's political conflict.
In the next phase, the Paris Peace Talks was another turning point in Cambodia's politics and also an important event in the political life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Paris Peace Agreement and the retirement of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk have become another new political discipline for Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian People's Party. Therefore, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian People's Party, which leads the government of the State of Cambodia and controls almost all the territory, must be ready to resist only the tripartite movement led by Samdech Norodom Sihanouk.
The complexities and difficulties before the election are already a major challenge for Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the face of responsibility within the party as the initiator of negotiations and reaching this election. But the results of the first election on May 23, 1993, in which the CPP won only 51 seats, lost to FUNCINPEC's FUNCINPEC party by seven seats, became another source of pressure for the tripartite negotiators. .
In order to avoid any internal problems of the party and any bloodshed, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to resign as Prime Minister, leaving the National Assembly of Cambodia to elect a new Prime Minister to replace Samdech. However, the intention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at that time was vehemently denied by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, who was then a loyal army chief.
After the rejection of these two loyal volunteers, the senior officials of the Cambodian state at that time considered and coordinated their internal affairs. As the CPP refused to accept the election results, the crisis resurfaced for Cambodia, which could not form a government to lead the country.
At this stage, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was under two major pressures: to fight against the power struggle to lead the state with the first Prime Minister, and to fight against the Khmer Rouge forces along the border. Which always causes constant aggression.
During the power struggle between the first and second prime ministers, many dangerous and life-threatening events took place in Samdech Techo Hun Sen. For example, on July 4, 1994, there was a plot to overthrow Samdech Techo Hun Sen and arrest him and imprison him in Prey Veng province.
The coup plot was orchestrated by former Minister of Interior Sin Song, former Deputy Minister of Interior Sin Sen and Prince Norodom Chakrapong, as well as some members of the armed forces. But this plan failed because Samdech Techo Hun Sen knew the plan beforehand and ordered the arrest of the masterminds of these coups.
On November 19, 1996, Kov Samuth, a police officer, husband, sister of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany and brother-in-law of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was shot dead in front of Boeung Keng Kang restaurant in central Phnom Penh.
However, this project was known to Samdech Techo Hun Sen in advance and alert. Finally, the clash occurred on July 5-6, 1997. The clashes, known as the "war of cooking", left the monks' forces defeated and dispersed as the monks left the country two days before the shooting.
After the clash, to ensure the functioning of the state, FUNCINPEC Minister of Foreign Affairs Ing Huot was facilitated by MPs and proposed to be the first Prime Minister to replace Norodom Ranariddh.
Despite attempts to take Samdech's life, in the spirit of national reconciliation and the desire to bring about national unity with the intervention of friendly countries, finally to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Cambodian people always have a heart That compassion also paved the way for Samdech Krom Preah and FUNCINPEC politicians to have the opportunity to return to the country.
What is noteworthy is that the second mandate election of FUNCINPEC party was cracked and divided internally. Many party officials went to form a new party. In this election campaign, both Samdech Krom Preah and Mr. Sam Rainsy campaigned on the topic of territorial sovereignty with Vietnam, such as the commemoration of the Cambodian-Vietnamese friendship, the abolition of the border agreement and the conquest of Khmer territory. Kampuchea Krom and so on.
The election campaign has three prominent political parties: the Cambodian People's Party, FUNCINPEC and the Sam Rainsy Party. Finally, the date of the second mandate election organized by the Royal Government of Cambodia itself reached July 26, 1998, with 39 political parties competing.
In this election, only three political parties won seats, including the CPP with 64 seats, FUNCINPEC with 43 seats and the SRP with 15 seats. The election results have stalled the formation of a new government, as the election law stipulates that the political party that can lead the government must have two-thirds of the seats in the National Assembly.
After months of political stalemate and protests, finally under the mediation of King Norodom Sihanouk, the then head of state and king, the three political parties agreed to take the oath of office. First time in Siem Reap on September 24, 1998.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that if at that time all four 40 bullets exploded all at once or that morning there was no heavy rain almost breaking the sky, which caused these control cables to cross the water, maybe Samdech's life would have ended. Since then. However, Samdech confirmed that he had already given agriculture to those who wanted to kill Samdech in Siem Reap, even though Samdech had the light to research.
In connection with the bombing, Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) spies found and charged 63-year-old Sok Yoeun, a Sam Rainsy Party activist. He also fled into Thai territory and was jailed by Thai authorities.
The agreement to form a new government, the second legislature of the National Assembly, has been commented on as causing Sam Rainsy, who is in Paris, very upset over the formation of the government without his knowledge. In particular, Samdech Krom Preah betrayed his promise with him from the beginning, "If you enter, you will enter together, if you do not enter, you will not enter together."
The formation of the Royal Government for the second mandate can be considered as the end of the situation and the black page of the political scene in Cambodia, because from 1998 onwards, the political situation in Cambodia is no longer serious. Although still hot, not as bad as before 1998.
In the 1990s, in addition to the political situation in the Royal Government, which caused a heavy rainstorm for the political life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the situation of the Khmer Rouge guerrillas who did not participate in the formation of the Royal Government under the power of the Paris Agreement is also a story. Leads to high memories in the history of political life and leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen as well.
Cambodia could not have progressed as long as the Khmer Rouge guerrillas continued to exist. Because the Khmer Rouge army always attacked and disrupted the achievements of the Royal Government in the 1990s. Seeing this, Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the first term of the Royal Government, even though he was the second Prime Minister, always sought to end the presence of the Khmer Rouge guerrillas.
In order to end the presence of the Khmer Rouge guerrillas, in addition to increasing the strategy of fighting by the armed forces, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always set out a strategy to negotiate with the Khmer Rouge leaders. Later, the strategy to end the presence of Khmer Rouge forces in the jungle was dubbed a "win-win" policy.
Starting from this policy, on September 14, 1996, Samdech Techo Hun Sen addressed Samdech Norodom Sihanouk, the then King and Head of State, to ask for a royal pardon for Ieng Sary, the Khmer Rouge leader. One man ruled Pailin, Samlot and Malai. Asking for a royal pardon for Ieng Sary was a tactic for Ieng Sary to secede from Pol Pot, Khieu Samphan, Nuon Chea, Son Sen, and Ta Mok, who ruled Anlong Veng and Preah Vihear.
After receiving a royal pardon from the King to increase the confidence of Ieng Sary and the Khmer Rouge, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to fly to Pailin to meet directly with Ieng Sary on August 23, 1996
This trip to the enemy area in Pailin is considered to be a brave and risky decision because going to Bailin is like entering a tiger cave. Samdech Techo Hun Sen had repeatedly reminded the trip to the Pailin area, his beloved mother and grandmother prevented him from going to the Khmer Rouge area.
In response to this prohibition, Samdech told his mother and grandmother: "If I go to die, I will die alone, but if I succeed, we will get the whole earth." Samdech's visit to Pailin increased the confidence of Ieng Sary and the Khmer Rouge under his rule and led to their secession.
In fact, the negotiation process to defeat the Khmer Rouge was expected to be successful soon, not until the end of 1998. However, due to the distrust of the coalition government, especially the FUNCINPEC party of Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh, the efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Cambodian People's Party with the Khmer Rouge were seen as stealing forces against them. Back.
Because of this suspicion, Samdech Krom Preah, through Mr. Nhek Bun Chhay, who was his army chief at the time, stole to open the Khmer Rouge negotiations at Anlong Veng and Preah Vihear and brought Khmer Rouge forces to the center. Phnom Penh. The actions of Samdech Krom Preah and FUNCINPEC Party led to an explosion of firecrackers on July 5-6, 1997.
A fierce battle in the center of Phnom Penh disbanded Samdech Krom Preah's forces, plus the death of Pol Pot in April 1998 and the defeat of Samdech Krom Preah in July 1998. The Khmer Rouge in Anlong Veng, the last base, exchanged views on Samdech Krom Preah and lost faith.
The Khmer Rouge in Anlong Veng also stopped the policy of tying the knot with Norodom Ranariddh and saw that the people who were honest, honest and faithful, serving the nation, religion, the king and the heroes of national unification and reconciliation were truly heroes of peace. And that there is always a tolerant policy and always open the opportunity for those who are wrong to correct themselves without impunity, only Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced to provide three properties: guarantee safety and life, guarantee career and occupation, and guarantee property protection.
For these reasons, the last remaining Khmer Rouge forces, including the entire Khmer Rouge cabinet, including former head of state Khieu Samphan, former parliamentary speaker Nuon Chea, Ieng Sary, Chan Youran, Chuon Choeun, and their families, traveled to Samdech's residence. Techo Hun Sen in Takhmao to surrender with the Royal Government of Cambodia on December 29, 1998. The Khmer Rouge was completely overthrown and the remaining forces were integrated.
December 29, 1998 is designated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a new day in the history of Cambodia to end the dark pages of Cambodia, end the flames of war, end the national division, bring back a new era of peace, national unity National reconciliation, national unity and territorial unity for the nation and the people of Cambodia in the last 500 years in the history of Cambodia.
After the complete success of national unification in line with the political crisis, it was eased after 1998, that is, from 2000, a new time for Samdech Techo Hun Sen to pay full attention to Build national development and national integration into the international community as well.
Since the fall of the Angkorian Empire in the twelfth century, Cambodia has known only the breakup, the war, the racism, the devastation and the decline, and its fame has been buried on the international stage. It can be said that only in the last 20 years, Cambodia has known the reunification of the nation and the rebuilding of its prestige in the international arena, full of national honor and pride for all Cambodians.
Through the political events and development of the society that has been tied to the life of Samdech Techo Hun Sen for more than 40 years, this is an indisputable fact that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a Cambodian son who Developed life from a farmer's son to a great statesman, a historical spy for the Cambodian nation.
