Living in Cambodia for 10 years, Lisa can speak a lot of Khmer and also made her love the country and the people of Cambodia.
Lisa is currently living in Phnom Penh and, like many other Cambodians, has already been vaccinated with two doses of Kovid 19 vaccine. On Monday, she vaccinated her 16-year-old son at the National Children's Hospital.
Speaking about the vaccination, Ms. Lisa praised the leadership of the Royal Government and the launch of a rapid vaccination plan for the people. She said the Royal Government of Cambodia has done better than her country, which so far has only vaccinated the elderly and given a small amount, while children have not had the opportunity to be vaccinated.
In addition to praising the management of vaccinations, Ms. Liza also praised the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen that has made many improvements.
Because of her work in rural education, Lisa has traveled to many provinces over the past 10 years. The Brazilian woman sees many developments in infrastructure as well as other areas.
Ms. Lisa praised the development in Cambodia, so "really change, change for the better. Now the good road has a very good place. "Ten years ago, I saw this government doing a lot for the Cambodian people."
Ms. Lisa also pointed out that with living in Cambodia for 10 years, she became attached to Cambodia and considered Cambodia as her home country. She rarely goes to her home country, although there is a family that provides warmth for her.
