Following is a statement from the Kampot provincial administration: India will send four warships to the South China Sea and other sensitive areas.
The Indian military is usually on high alert for actions that could upset China, but tensions have risen following clashes between the two countries' armies on the disputed border last year. According to a statement from the Indian Navy, four warships will be deployed for two months to Southeast Asia, the South China Sea and the western Pacific Ocean.
The Indian military said the move was to emphasize solidarity with friendly countries to ensure good maritime security. During the deployment, Indian warships will also take part in joint military exercises with the United States, Japan and Australia near Guam. China has already criticized the military exercise as "destabilizing" in the region.
The South China Sea has become one of the hotspots in Sino-US relations, with Washington frequently moving warships to the area.
