The following is the certificate of Stung Treng Provincial Administration: The Minister of Commerce defended 3 draft laws in the Senate
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, on the afternoon of August 3, 2021, led an inter-ministerial delegation to defend three draft laws in front of the Senate Standing Committee.
The Senate Standing Committee, chaired by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, held an online meeting to review three draft laws, including: Draft Law on the Approval of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (APEC) ), Draft Law on the Approval of the Free Trade Agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and China and the Draft Law on Competition.
The Minister also briefed the leadership of the Senate, the National Assembly and the expert committee on the content and key benefits of the three draft laws.
The Minister said that the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (AEC) is one of the largest free trade agreements in the region, with the participation of 10 ASEAN member countries and major trading partners. The five include China, Japan, Korea, New Zealand, Australia and Australia.
The deal could reach a market of 2.2 billion people, or 30 percent of the world's population, with a combined GDP of about $ 26.2 trillion, or 30 percent of the country's GDP. The world will account for about 28% of world trade (based on 2019 data).
The ASEAN Agreement is a comprehensive, high-quality, mutually beneficial agreement that will facilitate the expansion of regional trade and investment supply chains, signaling to the world about support. A multilateral free trade system based on the rule of law and, in particular, contributing to the rapid economic recovery of Cambodia and the region from the Kovid-19 crisis.
Minister Pan Sosak emphasized that based on the results of negotiations and studies of the Economic Research Institute for ASEAN and East Asia (ERIA), after the conclusion of the ASEAN Agreement, Cambodia may have an annual increase in exports. 7.3% invested 23.4% and GDP about 2% of current GDP.
Separately, the Law on the Approval of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement was mentioned by the Minister of Commerce that this agreement has opened up a bigger and better market for agricultural products, vegetables, fruits and processed products. And many other handicrafts and products while Cambodia can produce and comply with hygiene rules and standards.
This agreement can also get the flow of trade in services that Cambodia can export in case of skilled and qualified training, especially when Cambodia can strengthen itself in the service sector in the future. Provide more investment opportunities to Cambodia, which will provide opportunities for Cambodian businessmen who want to expand the market for services and goods to export more to the Chinese market.
After hearing the values of the three draft laws, the leaders of the Senate, the National Assembly and the leaders of the specialized committees expressed their full support for the three draft laws.
