In the first 7 months of this year, pepper exports reached more than 20,000 tons, more than 5 times
According to the report of the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the first seven months of 2021, Cambodia exported 22,580.68 tons of pepper, an increase of 558.19%.
Mr. Nguon Lay, President of Kampot Pepper Association, stated that although Kovid 19 disease continues to spread, the market situation of Kampot pepper has improved in terms of export because there are more companies to continue to order and demand from the people.
He added that the export of Kampot pepper from January to July 2021 is more than 60 tons. He added that the momentum of pepper exports this year has increased compared to last year.
He added that although the weather is not very good, but by July 2021, Kampot pepper exports increased compared to the previous year due to the company's export market has increased pepper orders from foreign customers as well. . As for the situation of Kampot pepper harvesting of farmers, some farmers have already harvested completely, some have harvested 80% and some have just harvested 60 to 70%.
He said that the current price of pepper is the same, with black pepper at $ 15 per kilogram, red pepper at $ 25 per kilogram and white pepper at $ 28 per kilogram.
