(Kandal): After Chan Vito, a police officer at the Ministry of Interior, ordered his children to cut off public roads and prevent people from traveling, the group of 143 people asked Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province, to help solve this problem. .
He said that this road they use to travel to fish fishing, picking lotus, picking lotus and lotus leaves in Boeung Thom, as well as travel to the shrines of Kampong Rotes, Koh Lias and Koh Sleng floating since ancient times. Even the authorities acknowledge that there have never been any problems, and in the past, because the road was low and flooded, it was difficult for people to travel.
He added that suddenly, on July 19, Mr. Chan Vito, the owner of the sand dredging business near this road, ordered his children to take Eskawa off this road, making it impossible for them to travel. They lodged complaints with Chheu Teal commune hall and Kien Svay district hall.
He claimed that only on the afternoon of July 31, 2021, the district authorities led the machine to clear the road again, but was later stopped by officials said that there was intervention from higher levels. If this road is cut off, they have no way to go to the lake to make a living and can not go to the shrine, so please intervene for traders to clear the road as before.
