Some people in Angkor Thom district have not yet been vaccinated, Mr. Sar Thavy called on the authorities to urge the remaining people to be vaccinated
(Siem Reap): More than 3,000 people in Angkor Thom district, Siem Reap province have not yet been vaccinated against Kovid 19. Lt. Gen. Thavy, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Angkor Thom District Vaccination Coordination Team, called on the authorities to encourage those who have not been vaccinated to get vaccinated.
The Ministry of National Defense Vaccination Team started the first 19 doses of Kovid vaccination for people in Angkor Thom district on July 16, 2021. The first 19 cases of Kovid vaccination were completed last week.
During this week's vaccination review meeting, Lt. Gen. Thavy said that about 17,863 people in Angkor Thom district had been vaccinated. But only 15,400 people came to be vaccinated.
According to the data, more than 2,000 people have not yet been vaccinated. During the vaccination review meeting, Lt. Gen. Thavy, who was on hand to facilitate the vaccination, asked local authorities to help find those who had not been vaccinated and to encourage them to get vaccinated.
"It is unfortunate that our people did not come to be vaccinated. We need to continue to educate, guide and encourage them to vaccinate everyone. "If we do not inject them into everyone, we will not be able to build community immunity to fight Kovid 19." This was stated by Lt. Gen. Thavy in the meeting to review the work.
However, Mr. Sar Thavy assessed that the first phase of vaccination against Kovid 19 for nearly 20 days in Angkor Thom district achieved remarkably good results.
As the Chairman of the Vaccination Coordinating Committee, Mr. Sar Thavy praised the Vaccination Team of the Sub-Committee on Vaccination of the Ministry of National Defense for its diligent efforts in vaccinating the people.
Mr. Sar Thavy also thanked the local authorities at all levels for facilitating the vaccination work, thanking the people, workers who participated in supporting the national vaccination campaign of the local administration and went to get vaccinated in large numbers.
