It is difficult to just look at one part of the diet and link it to a health condition because there are many areas that can play a role in health issues. Recent studies have found a possible link between coffee and reduced mortality.
Coffee can give you some resistance, such as:
However, coffee can still be dangerous because it is high in caffeine. For example, it can temporarily raise blood pressure. Women who are pregnant or want to become pregnant or are breastfeeding should not consume caffeine. Drinking uncooked brewed coffee also raises cholesterol levels slightly.
Your coffee drinking habits are a good thing and can be beneficial as well. But if you have side effects from coffee, such as heartburn, anxiety or sleep deprivation, you should reduce your coffee intake.
Royal Government Establishes National Committee for Community Management and Development of Tourism and Ecotourism
In Sub-Decree No. 125 dated July 30, 2021, the above-mentioned general provision states that the establishment of the National Committee for Management and Development of Community-Based Tourism and Ecotourism is to lead and promote the development of community-based tourism and ecotourism. Across Cambodia.
The National Committee for Management and Development of Community-Based Tourism and Ecotourism is chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment as Permanent Vice-Chairman, and Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries as Vice-Chairman. Relevant institutions together with the Provincial Board of Governors are members.
In the new sub-decree, it is stated that the NCDD As a staff to the Royal Government with the following roles and responsibilities:
Prepare and update national strategic policies and plans for community development, tourism and ecotourism
* Prepare the necessary legal documents to manage the tourism community and ecotourism
* Lead, coordinate, cooperate and promote the development of tourism and ecotourism communities to contribute to the development of Cambodia's tourism sector.
* Lead, coordinate and monitor the implementation of the National Ecotourism Policy (2019-2030) and strategic plans related to the promotion of community-based tourism and ecotourism development.
* Examine, evaluate and recognize the request for recognition of community-based tourism and ecotourism
* Review, evaluate and approve projects implemented by the community, national and international organizations in the tourism and ecotourism community
* Monitor and monitor the operation of community-based tourism and ecotourism development projects
* Organize the annual National Ecotourism Forum and events to promote the development of tourism and ecotourism communities.
* Awareness and promotion of community-based tourism and ecotourism
* Provide necessary technical assistance to communities and operators in community tourism and ecotourism
* Awarding incentive logos to community tour operators and investors in community-based tourism and ecotourism development projects
* Collaborate with ministries, institutions, national and international organizations, the private sector and all stakeholders to facilitate the development of Cambodia's tourism community and ecotourism effectively.
Perform other duties as assigned by the Royal Government.
Please be informed that under the leadership of Minister Thong Khon in the mechanism of this inter-ministerial working group, the main work has been accomplished as follows:
* The Royal Government has set November 19 every year to hold the National Ecotourism Forum, with the first National Ecotourism Forum in 2019 under the chairmanship of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and the second in January 2021 under the chairmanship. Minister Thong Khon on behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
Five key inter-ministerial working group meetings are held to address the real challenges facing communities across the country.
In fact, the decision of the Royal Government to establish this National Committee is really political and strategic, with the work to promote the development of community-based tourism and ecotourism with inter-sectoral and inter-institutional interface, which is necessary to expand the work. Closer cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions at both the national and sub-national levels.
