The Cambodia Securities Exchange is licensed by the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to operate as a securities market operator, securities clearing and settlement operator and securities operator. Currently, the types of securities that can be listed and traded on the CSX. Includes equity securities (shares) and bonds (bonds), which are the original securities issued by local companies.
Investing in a company's stock makes the investor a shareholder in that company, and investing in bonds makes the investor a creditor. Derivatives, which are valuable securities based on the value of the original securities, such as precious metals, currencies, interest rates, stocks and indices, are not traded on the CSX. And in the past, the use of the word "stock" or "stock" to refer to these derivatives was incorrect.
