(Phnom Penh): Although Cambodia and China have been severely affected by the Kovid 19 crisis, the bilateral trade volume between the two countries reached nearly 5 billion US dollars, up 31% in the first six months of the year. This 2021. This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
According to Mr. Sok Sopheak, given the volume of bilateral trade between Cambodia and China for the first six months of 2021, although the two countries have been severely affected by the 19-crisis crisis, trade growth remains. There is an increase.
He pointed out that Cambodia generally exports to China garments, shoes, leather, fur, machinery, pistons, rice, rubber, bananas, cassava, cashew nuts, shoes, suitcases, etc.
Mr. Sok Sopheak stated that, seeing the huge potential of trade, the Royal Government of Cambodia and China have set a total trade target for 2023 to achieve 10 billion US dollars.
