(Phnom Penh): In a meeting between the ASEAN Foreign Ministers and representatives of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (AICHR) held on the occasion of the 54th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting on August 2, 2021, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation stated that respect for human rights must be comprehensive and not double standards.
Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also stressed the need to distinguish between respect for human rights and freedom to promote harmony and progress of humanity from the fraudulent use of these sacred principles to incite hatred. Social instability and interference in the internal affairs of other countries.
"Awareness and respect for human rights must be comprehensive, without double standards, and respect the national sovereignty of each country in accordance with the principle of non-interference in internal affairs," he said.
At the meeting, the ASEAN Foreign Ministers stressed the importance of the commitment to adhere to the human rights agenda, including the protection and promotion of the core freedoms of the people of ASEAN.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers also urged the AICHR to be more active in the task of promoting and protecting human rights throughout ASEAN, especially during the difficult period caused by the Kovid-19 outbreak.
