The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) was established on August 8, 1967, 53 years ago. If Timor-Leste could become a member of ASEAN, Timor-Leste would become the 11th member of the 10-nation Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN).
