General knowledge: Flowers represent the 10 ASEAN member countries
(Phnom Penh): The 10 ASEAN member countries have chosen one or more of their national flowers, while each of them has its own unique characteristics, including smell and color, meaning, national cause, relationship with culture and people's way of life. Here are the flowers representing the 10 ASEAN member countries:
The romduol flower is the national flower of Cambodia, one of the most beautiful ornaments since ancient times. This type of flower is grown almost all over Cambodia, both in the forest and in the village. Its flowers are yellow, the petals are thick, and the eyes are full of fancy flowers.
Khmer people consider Romduol flower to be compared to Khmer women (Khmer women) who have good manners, gentle, gentle, beautiful and beautiful. Cambodians, both in the country and in neighboring countries, often use this flower in their wedding ceremonies or religious ceremonies, such as weddings, Krong Pali ceremonies, prayers, as well as various ceremonies.
The romduol flower is also closely associated with the aesthetics, design, culture, art, music, architecture of the Cambodian people. Angkor Wat and so on.
Angkor Hospital for Children Holds Solidarity Flower Festival Online to Raise Funds to Support Children's Treatments
(Siem Reap): Angkor Hospital for Children will host its 8th annual Solidarity Flower Festival online during the 19th Kovid Crisis.
The 19-year Kovid Crisis has continued to plague Angkor Hospital for Children financially, as a large number of fundraising events or activities have not been able to take place, and fundraisers, businesses or philanthropists have been able to provide assistance. Hospitalization also declined sharply.
Angkor Hospital for Children has adapted to the new context of the 8th Solidarity Flower Festival to raise funds for the hospital for the first time during this difficult time.
According to the press release of Angkor Hospital for Children, the above ceremony will be held in two sessions, the first part is a sermon program as a sermon and the dissemination of the news of the festival online by well-known monks in and Abroad on the Facebook page of Angkor Hospital for Children from 9 to 10 am every day from 13 to 28 August 2021 with different good topics.
The second session will take place on August 29, with a limited number of participants in accordance with the rules of health during the 19-year period of Kovid. The program of sermons by 7 monks on "The Seven Noble Truths" is the culmination of the festival.
Seeing the hardships of the hospital, including Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem, the Royal Highness and the Chief Bishop of Wat Reachbo, decided to join as a initiator of the Solidarity Festival to help promote this event and raise funds through the network of Unconditionally.
Dr. Nguon Chanpheaktra, Director of Angkor Hospital for Children, also called on Cambodian philanthropists, both local and foreign, to continue to participate in all forms, such as sharing personal funds, donating to the event or helping to spread the word about the festival. On social media.
He also stated that "the money received from the organization of the Silver Flower Festival is the most important part to maintain the process of providing medical, life-saving care services for Cambodian children with quality, compassionate and free of charge. In Angkor Hospital for Children.
