Full-day mission: Samdech Techo's gift was handed over to 100-year-old grandparents who volunteered to vaccinate Kovid 19 in Takeo, Kampot and Koh Kong provinces.
(Takeo-Kampot-Koh Kong): On the whole day of August 2, 2021, Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, Chairman of the Commission for Kovid 19 Vaccination, brought a gift from Samdech Techo Hun The Prime Minister of Cambodia presents three 100-year-old grandparents with their own hands.
Hundreds of kilometers from Phnom Penh, Ms. O Vandin brought this gift to grandparents in Takeo, Kampot and Koh Kong provinces, including:
Speaking on the occasion of handing over gifts to grandparents, Ms. O Vandin always brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the grandparents and asked about their health status after Get vaccinated against Kovid 19 as well.
Although he is 100 years old, his health is still good and he is very grateful to the Prime Minister for his efforts to find a vaccine for the people of Kovid 19 and they themselves. Received the vaccine, plus the prince's gift.
Answering Ms. Vandin's question regarding the health condition after the vaccination, the three grandparents described that their health was good, there was no difference, just normal eating and accommodation. Daily.
Interestingly, a 100-year-old woman living in Sangkat Smach Meanchey, Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province, who had been vaccinated against Kovid 19 in both doses, claimed that she had low back pain and could not wake up. Grandma's chronic illness suddenly disappeared after being vaccinated against Kovid.
Ms. Hong Lach said that in the past, she had a chronic illness, back pain and joint pain, sometimes can not sleep, but this disease suddenly disappeared after her. 19 vaccinated against Kovid.
She added that the Kovid 19 vaccine was not left in her body, but she was very happy when the government allowed her to be vaccinated against Kovid 19. She said that when she was injected, she was very worried about this deadly disease and did not dare to go anywhere.
Please be informed that last weekend, Ms. O Vandin also led the team to travel thousands of kilometers day and night to take the gift of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to the elderly grandparents. For the past 100 years, they have volunteered to vaccinate 19 against measles in Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Siem Reap, Preah Vihear and Kampong Thom provinces. Mondulkiri Province Announces 4 Kovid Patients and 8 Cured
