(Phnom Penh): On August 2, 2021, the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) organized a pre-departure orientation ceremony for 14 Cambodian government officials selected to receive scholarships. Master's degree for the academic year 2021-2023.
With a mission to support the development of human resources (HRD) with partner countries, KOICA invites talented Cambodian civil servants and helps them develop the professional skills and knowledge that play an important role in Cambodia.
As part of KOICA's "Capacity Building and Capacity Building for the Future" program, the program aims to share Korean experiences and knowledge with foreign government officials, giving them the opportunity to study areas of interest in the Republic of Korea. .
The KOICA Scholarship Program is a fully funded program supported by the Government of the Republic of Korea to KOICA partner countries. The scholarship program has been in Cambodia since 1994 and aims to share Korean development experiences with Cambodia to contribute to Cambodia's long-term development needs.
To achieve this mission, KOICA has launched Master's Degree Scholarships with 20 prestigious universities in Korea in agriculture, rural development, education, governance, technology and environment and energy. In particular, for 2021, there are 14 outstanding officials who have received scholarships for master's degree courses with eight famous universities in Korea.
Mr. No Hyun Joon welcomed and congratulated the scholarship officials. He added that KOICA has pledged to continue to assist Cambodia in strengthening the capacity of its officers through the provision of scholarships and additional training, despite the threat of Kovid-19.
Mr. M. Sour encouraged the scholarship officials to seize this great opportunity to learn about the development of Korea during their stay in Korea and to share their knowledge, skills and experiences with other Cambodians by following Lessons learned through this master's program on their work for the sustainable socio-economic development of Cambodia.
In this event, KOICA Office in Cambodia gave a brief presentation on the master's degree program and provided scholarship officers with basic orientation such as: KOICA Scholarship Guidelines, Second: Tips for Living in Korea , 3: Information about the Cambodia-Korea Alumni Association and 4: Ethics on Integrity and Sexual Harassment.
Scholarship Recipients thanked and commended their support to the KOICA Office and the Government of Korea, as well as their commitment to bringing about social and policy reforms in Cambodia after Learn from the experience of Korea.
