South Korea's Defense Ministry said in a statement that Seoul and Washington were discussing military exercises, but no final decision had been made. According to the South Korean Defense Ministry, the two allies will make a decision after considering a number of factors, including the issue of COVID-19 and the issue of supporting diplomatic efforts to build lasting peace on the Korean Peninsula.
South Korea's Unification Ministry, which is in charge of inter-Korean affairs, said joint military exercises between South Korea and the United States should not be a source of military tensions with North Korea under any circumstances.
Seoul and Washington regularly hold joint military exercises, mainly during the spring and summer seasons. While the two allies claim that such military exercises are to strengthen their joint defense capabilities, North Korea has always been outspoken in its criticism of it as a war exercise for aggression.
On Sunday, Kim Yoo-jong, the half-sister of North Korean leader Kim Jong-un and a senior official in the country's ruling party, warned Seoul that South Korea's joint military exercises And the United States will undermine relations-building efforts.
