Kim Jong Un's sister leaves South Korea to choose between restoring ties or conducting exercises with US
SEOUL: The sister of North Korean leader Kim Jong Un, Kim Yoo-jong, has warned that if South Korea holds joint military exercises with the United States as planned, efforts to restore ties between the two Koreas will continue. Both may be destroyed. This was quoted from Reuters on Monday afternoon, August 2, 2021.
Kim Yoo-jung's warning comes as North and South Korea are in the crucial stages of resuming talks. South Korean President Park Geun-hye on Tuesday announced that South and North Korea had reconnected a hotline that Pyongyang cut off a year ago when relations deteriorated. The two countries have been working to restore ties.
"Our government and military are closely monitoring the situation," Kim Yoo-jong said in a statement released by North Korea's state-run KCNA last weekend. "Whether South Korea will participate in military exercises with the United States or make a big decision ... hopeful or hopeless, it is not up to us."
The United States and South Korea are scheduled to hold joint military exercises this August. North Korea has often condemned and accused military exercises of preparing for its invasion.
