(Pursat): Authorities decided to cremate the body of a victim who was found floating in the river, which was swollen and rotten and no relatives knew.
This incident caused a surprise at 12:30 on July 31, 2021 at the point of Pursat River from top to bottom in Ta Sdey village, Veal commune, Kandeang district, Pursat province.
Sources from the competent authorities said that the body of the victim who was floating in the river was not identified, but it was known that the man was about 30 years old, black, 1.6 meters tall, wearing a long-sleeved T-shirt and a T-shirt. In yellow, short sleeves, wearing black pants.
The source added that based on the forensic examination of the expert doctor and the specialized unit of the Scientific Technical Police Office of the Pursat Provincial Police Commission, 19 corpses were tested on the corpse, the result was (negative). Later, the technical and scientific office, including a team of doctors, examined the body and found no suspicious marks related to the criminal case.
Experts and experts from the Office of Science and Technology have speculated that the body may have died as a result of the gusts of wind falling into the river.
At present, the bodies of the victims have been requested by the Pursat Provincial Prosecutor to be cremated according to the Buddhist tradition at the riverside in Ta Sdey village, Veal commune, Kandieng district, Pursat province.
