Afghanistan: Flight delayed after rocket crashes in Kandahar airport
KABUL (Reuters) - A flight at Kandahar airport in Afghanistan was delayed Sunday morning after rockets hit the second major international airport in South Asia. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Sunday, August 1, 2021.
According to Afghan officials, the Taliban fired three rockets at Kandahar International Airport, two of which crashed into the runway on Saturday night. There were no immediate reports of casualties, and the Taliban have not commented on the allegations as they escalate their offensive from Kabul.
On Saturday, three civilians were killed and 10 others, including two women and two children, were wounded in fighting between the Taliban and Kabul government forces in Kabul. Kandahar.
