This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen took his grandchildren to be vaccinated and announced the launch of a vaccination campaign for children between the ages of 12 and under 18.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of Sunday, August 1, 2021, 2021, announced the opening of the Kovid 19 vaccination campaign for children and adolescents aged 12 to under 18 years old.
With the announcement of this campaign to give people the confidence to bring their children to be vaccinated, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, will also bring about 11 grandchildren of Samdech aged 12 to under 18 to be vaccinated. Vaccines, too.
In addition to Samdech's grandchildren, the grandchildren of leaders and other high-ranking government officials will also start vaccinating tomorrow. It is remembered that when Cambodia started the first vaccination campaign for 18-year-olds on February 10, Samdech Techo also assigned his children and the children of the leaders to vaccinate like this. Well.
Taking children and grandchildren to lead vaccinations is seen as giving confidence and encouraging people to believe in the value of vaccines and getting children vaccinated.
It is for this reason that Cambodia has launched an action plan for vaccinating 19 cases of Kovid 19 against children and adolescents aged 12 to under 18, in addition to the population aged 18 and over. About 10 million people.
In the action plan for vaccinating 19 children and adolescents, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that vaccinating children and young people will be another new opportunity for the Royal Government to expand its coverage. The Kovid-19 vaccine will be given to more people to protect the lives of the people and to build community resilience throughout Cambodia.
The campaign to vaccinate about 2 million children and adolescents under the age of 12 will start in Phnom Penh first, then continue in Kandal, Sihanoukville, Koh Kong and other provinces.
