He said that Cambodia is proud of the park officials who have sacrificed their physical and mental strength and sometimes risked their lives for the cause of the environment and natural resources. The beautiful natural scenery that you have visited in the protected areas comes from the tireless efforts of day and night to patrol, enforce the law, crack down on all kinds of natural resource crimes, education and dissemination.
During the first six months of 2021, from January to June 2021, park rangers patrolled the protected areas and biodiversity corridors a total of 14,422 times, including cracking down on 4 natural resource crimes. 238 cases. Park rangers seized 2,462 chainsaws, confiscated 182 cars, 308 bulldozers, 336 motorbikes, 24 tractors and 1,260 cubic meters of timber.
At the same time, park rangers and community members protected 25,596 traps and 348 firearms.
