Accounting and Auditing Regulatory Authority announces the postponement of the submission of the audited financial statements for the year 2020 online for obligatory enterprises
(Phnom Penh): The Accounting and Auditing Regulator on July 30, 2021 issued a notification on the delay in submitting the audited financial statements for the year 2020 online for obligatory enterprises.
As of July 30, 2021, many enterprises have completed their obligations to submit their audited 2020 financial statements, according to a statement obtained by Fresh News today. Accounting and Auditing Regulators.
At the same time, some enterprises have accessed the E-Filing system to submit the audited 2020 financial statements, but have not yet completed the final procedure, need more time.
Given the practical issues mentioned above, the Accounting and Auditing Regulators would like to extend the time for enterprises to submit their audited 2020 financial statements by the following deadlines:
1: By August 9, 2021: For enterprises that have already accessed the system and need more time to complete the procedure.
2: By September 10, 2021: For enterprises that have been experiencing technical problems that can not access the E-Filing system. In the meantime, the technical team of the Accounting and Auditing Regulators will make additional work to help solve the problems of those enterprises.
Separately, enterprises that have been authorized to complete the work of independent audit and publish independent audit opinion must comply with the date set in the response letter of the Accounting and Auditing Regulator.
