(Kampong Chhnang): Officials from the Production and Veterinary Office of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture vaccinated cattle and buffaloes of people suffering from tuberculosis in some communes in Boribo and Teuk Phos districts of Kampong Chhnang province. The vaccination took place on the morning of July 29, 2021.
Mr. Hun Ly, Deputy Director of Procurement and Veterinary Office of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that after receiving reports from people in some communes in Boribo and Teuk Phos districts about cattle cases. Their symptoms were strange, with lumps on the skin, officials went to check and treat people to get rid of infectious diseases to cattle, which is also an important traction.
He added that veterinary officials visited the local area and disseminated the prevention of tumors by inspecting 15 families with 49 cows in Anchanh Rong commune, Boribo district. Thirty-seven cows were found to have lumps.
During the vaccination, the deputy director of the office called on people to take care of and monitor the health of cattle and clean the cages and feed properly to avoid any symptoms. If there are any symptoms on cattle that are suspicious, immediately report to the authorities to intervene in time.
He added that the production and veterinary office of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Agriculture continues to inspect livestock in other districts as the rainy season continues. Cambodian Foreign Minister to Attend the 54th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings within the ASEAN Framework from August 2-6
