(Kratie): Some people in Kratie province are still gathering to gamble without fear of the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
On July 30, 2021, villagers in Thom village, Sandan commune, Sambo district, Kratie province reported to Fresh News some abusive acts of villagers gathering to gamble, which is one of the reasons facing the epidemic. Kovid's disease 19.
In Thom village, Sandan commune, Sambo district, Kratie province, three people were found to be infected with Kovid 19. Among them, it is reported that there are also people who like to gamble.
Immediately after receiving the report, Kratie Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Lon Sophat ordered and instructed the police force of Sandan commune police station to search for the gambler.
Sandan commune administrative police force, in cooperation with the people, went to the house of Puch Lima, a 28-year-old female, and instructed and educated her not to gather and stop gambling.
The police force also advised them to understand the risk of contracting Kovid 19 and to participate in the implementation of the measures of the Ministry of Health, especially "3 do not and 3 prevent".
Apart from the main villages and other villages in the communes and districts, there are also reports that people are still gathering to gamble, leading to concerns about the spread of Kovid 19.
Lt. Gen. Lon Sophat confirmed that the police force always educates and advises people not to gather or gamble, which is against the law, especially in the face of the spread of Kovid 19. But because the police force in each commune is small and people often gather in secret places to play, it is difficult to find them.
He called on residents to report to the local police force when they see gambling rallies to help curb gambling and prevent the spread of Kovid 19. And youth with call for attention to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 (Video inside)
