(Phnom Penh): In the first six months of 2021, Cambodia exported to Thailand about 516 million US dollars, down 33 percent, while imports from Thailand amounted to more than 3.466 million US dollars. This is according to the report of the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand.
The trade volume between the two countries in the first six months of 2021 reached a total of 3.982 million US dollars, down 1% compared to the same period in 2020 of 4.025 million US dollars.
Pen Sovicheat, undersecretary of state and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, had previously stated that the decline in Cambodia's exports to Thailand was due to the Kovid-19 epidemic.
Mr. Pen Sovichet stated that "the decline in Cambodia's exports to Thailand may be due to the spread of Kovid-19 in the provinces along the Thai-Cambodian border, which has led to restrictions on transportation. "Freight between the two countries."
In addition, Mr. Pen Sovicheat also said that the decline in exports of Cambodian goods to Thailand is not due to declining consumer demand.
