Ministry of Labor raises 4 reasons and safety solutions to explain to Cambodian workers working in Thailand
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has mentioned four safety reasons and solutions to Cambodian workers working and staying in Thailand to explain to them to keep quiet in the same place, that is, not to move out of place. Stay at the Cambodian-Thai border, as this risky trip can actually increase the risk of transmission and transmission of Kovid-19, especially the new Delta mutation.
These four reasons and security solutions are stated in the announcement of the Ministry of Labor on the cooperation to suspend the travel or mobility from the accommodation of Cambodian workers who are staying and working in Thailand to the Cambodian-Thai border for a period of time. 14 days, officially released on July 30, 2021.
According to these measures, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has informed Cambodian workers who are staying and working in Thailand with four reasons and solutions:
1: Do not move from your current place of residence to the Cambodian-Thai border for 14 days from July 30 to August 12, 2021. If there is a necessary business or work to return to Cambodia, please wait until after August 12.
2. If workers travel to the Cambodian-Thai border by any means, they will be required to travel back to their original place. The owner of the car or the broker who incited or transported the workers violated the Thai authorities' ban and also faces legal action.
