(Kampong Speu): A two-star military officer named Soy Chansoeun, who violently abused and detained a woman, has been arrested by Kampong Speu Provincial Police on a warrant issued by the Kampong Speu Provincial Court. This is according to Major General Sam Samoun, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Speu, confirmed to Fresh Nesw on July 30, 2021.
The military officer, Soy Chansoeun, is a lieutenant general and serves as deputy director of the Development Command of the Ministry of National Defense. He was charged with "aggravated assault and illegal detention" of a woman named Duong Hemalis on January 26, 2021.
The commissioner confirmed that his police force had detained the military officer on a court arrest warrant. At this time, interrogation is underway for further action.
According to the story, on January 22, 2021, at 9:00 AM, the victim, Duong Hemalis, 41 years old, and Soy Chansoeun drove together to the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie with Soy Chansoeun as the driver. As the car approached the Takhmao roundabout, Soy Chansoeun and Duong Hemalis argued.
After leaving the hospital, Duong Hemalis came to file a complaint with the Kampong Speu Provincial Prosecutor for legal action. The above acts are offenses: Intentional violence with aggravating circumstances and illegal detention committed in Takhmao City, Kandal Province and in Kampong Speu Province on January 22, 2021 in accordance with the provisions of Article 218 and Article 253, point 1 of the Penal Code. 1 million doses of Sinovak vaccine will arrive in Cambodia tomorrow, July 31
