China calls US 'biggest peacemaker' after seven warships sail across Taiwan Strait
BEIJING: After US naval vessels crossed the Taiwan Strait again this week, the Chinese Defense Ministry reacted strongly, condemning the act as provocative and dangerous. This was released by Sputnik on Friday, July 30, 2021.
Chinese military spokesman Shi Yi said in a statement on Thursday that "frequent similar provocative actions by the United States clearly show that the United States is a destroyer of peace." "And the biggest stabilizer in the Taiwan Strait and also the biggest security risk maker in the region."
According to Xi, the USS Benfold was tracked by China's maritime and air forces as it crossed the Taiwan Strait between China and Taiwan on Wednesday. This. A Chinese military spokesman stressed that the Chinese military is ready to respond to threats and provocations and is committed to defending China's national sovereignty and territorial integrity.
It should be noted that the Beijing government considers Taiwan as only one of China's provinces, so the dispute between the two sides is a purely internal matter. China considers any foreigner interfering in this matter to be interfering in its internal affairs, which is absolutely unacceptable.
So far, in 2021, the United States has mobilized a total of seven naval vessels to cross the Taiwan Strait. Last year, a total of 15 US troops crossed the strait, up from nine in 2019. Kampot Provincial Administration Establishes Two Commissions to Prevent Mineral Exploitation and Illegal Fisheries Crimes
