Representative of lawyer Ky Tech presents Preah Vossa candles, gifts and suffixes to monks waiting for Preah Vossa at 20 pagodas in Bati district, Takeo province
Preah Ratanavisutthi Dhammaphong Minh said that the Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to learn the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings.
The rainy season festival is to arrange a holiday somewhere or in a pagoda for three months during the rainy season and not to travel far beyond the day and night, unless there is an important task. Necessary, such as parents who are seriously ill or invited to perform dharma, etc., determined to return within 7 days.
Traditionally, Buddhists bring gifts such as rice, candles, incense, oil, sbong, chivor, sak, and other items to the monks at the pagoda to supply them during the rainy season.
In addition to food and drink, Cambodians also donated rain to the monks, because we believe that the light of a candle helps to illuminate the future of the nation to be bright, beautiful and prosperous by good deeds, goodness, and they must keep the candle light. Keep burning for 3 months. On the other hand, this helps the pagoda to have candles used to light at night as well.
Please note that Preah Vossa candles, gifts and suffixes to be given to monks who are waiting for the rain at 20 pagodas now, each pagoda receives a large pair of Preah Vossa candles, orange juice, fruit juice, tea and sugar. A set of pure water, fish, noodles, 200 kg of rice and some suffixes.
