(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed the view that Kovid-19 is a major discipline in the test of steel friendship between Cambodia and China.
At the Second Closing Ceremony of the Cambodia-China Brain Bank on the afternoon of July 28, 2021, Dr. Kin Phea said that Cambodia is facing serious challenges due to the spread of Kovid-19 China As a strong friend, we have done our best to work with Cambodia to fight this epidemic.
He added that the efforts of the Chinese ally to help Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19 not only embody the special ties between the two sides, but also China's responsibility in building the Cambodian community. - China, which has a common future as well.
Day by day, year after year, Cambodia-China relations are gradually strengthened and expanded as strategic partners in all areas, as a community with a common destiny as a steel friend and as a good brotherly friendship. This is what Dr. Kin Phea further highlighted is the relationship between Cambodia and China.
According to Dr. Kin Phea, despite this, external enemies do not really want to see the development of relations between the two countries, they always fabricate stories and set up scenes to tarnish the reputation and relations between the two countries. . In this sense, China must help Cambodia to become a model country for development due to its good and deep relations with China.
Since the first outbreak of Kovid 19 in Wuhan, China, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has led a special delegation to visit Chinese President Xi Jinping as a steel friend. Many countries are afraid.
Such actions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen have also been called by Chinese journalists "handsome men walking in reverse." This means that everyone is scared and wants to evacuate the people of their country from China, but Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen did not do so and called on the people to remain silent and listen to the instructions of the authorities. There.
Later, Cambodia also had an outbreak of Kovid 19, and at that time, China also sent a series of equipment to fight Kovid 19, and also sent a team of Chinese medical experts. Even more so.
Until the 19th Kovid vaccination, Cambodia also became the first country to receive the vaccine from China for vaccination. Currently, the vaccines being given to Cambodians are overwhelmingly produced by Chinese companies, with both assistance and orders.
As of July 22, 2021, Cambodia has received a total of 17 million doses of vaccine. Through this vaccine, Cambodia has already achieved immunization of more than 6.4 million people, which is 64.55% of the target of about 10 million people to be vaccinated. The vast majority of vaccines that Cambodia currently has are Chinese vaccines, with both aid and orders.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has also announced that Cambodia will use the Chinese giant as a backbone on the supply of Kovid 19 vaccine. Similarly, in the past, the Chinese government has announced its firm stance to help Cambodia fight the Kovid 19 disease successfully.
Chinese Ambassador Wang Wintian once emphasized that China and Cambodia are good brothers and sisters, like arms and legs, and good friends who always help each other. As long as Kovid disease in Cambodia is not over, Chinese aid to Cambodia cannot be stopped. In the fight against smallpox, the Chinese people continue to support the Cambodian people.
