(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, on July 28, 2021, requested China to expedite internal procedures for the ratification of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement for this Agreement to enter into force. At the beginning of 2022.
This request was made on the occasion of Mr. Sok Sopheak's participation in the 2nd Cambodia-China Brain Bank High Level Forum: Towards a new stage in the development of Cambodia-China bilateral relations via video today. July 28, 2021.
Mr. Sok Sopheak stated that "the Chinese side should speed up the internal procedures for the ratification of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement so that this agreement enters into force in early 2022 to provide opportunities for traders and investors to download "The benefits of this agreement as soon as possible."
Mr. Sok Sopheak emphasized that this agreement will provide more investment opportunities to Cambodia in the field of services and exports more diverse, as well as provide opportunities for Chinese businessmen to invest in Cambodia.
According to Mr. Sok Sopheak, considering the volume of bilateral trade between Cambodia and China for the first six months of 2021, although the two countries have been severely affected by the Kovid 19 crisis, trade growth There is still a 31% increase in the value of nearly 5 billion US dollars, compared to the same six-month period in 2020, which is worth only 3.7 billion US dollars.
In general, Cambodia exports to China garments, shoes, leather, fur, machinery, pistons, rice, rubber, bananas, cassava, cashew nuts, shoes, suitcases, and re-imports from China products for investment and production, such as woven fabrics, cotton fabrics. Metal, construction materials, equipment and electronics, plastics, aluminum, furniture and paper and cardboard.
