(Phnom Penh): To promote and facilitate the capacity building of institutions and institutions to create harmony in the workplace, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and the American Center for International Labor Solidarity (ACILS) have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU). ) Held on the morning of July 28, 2021 in order to establish a framework for technical cooperation between the parties in order to contribute to the implementation of policies related to the field of labor.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that this Memorandum of Understanding will be another important framework of cooperation between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and ACILS, which will contribute to the implementation of the principles. The policy of the Royal Government in the development of the employment sector in Cambodia.
"Through this framework of cooperation, we will jointly strengthen the implementation of labor-related policies to meet the objectives set out in the memorandum to be signed," he said.
At the same time, the Minister also expressed his appreciation for the remarkable achievements gained from the cooperation under the framework of the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding in the past, including:
First, organize two tripartite study visits to the United States in August 2018 and October 2018 to exchange experiences related to the implementation of trade union rights in the hotel and casino sector related to collective bargaining methods.
Second, traffic safety education while traveling to workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector, especially to educate workers to understand and participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
Third, the provision of technical assistance through unions to amend the law on unions.
Fourth, strengthening the capacity of unions through the organization of training courses related to the legal field, especially the law on unions, the law on the National Social Security Fund and other regulations.
ACILS Program Director for Cambodia also praised the cooperation between the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and ACILS, which has worked hard together in the past to achieve excellent results.
He hoped that by renewing the MoU, both sides would show a willingness to further strengthen cooperation for the benefit of workers and contribute to the promotion of rights, working conditions and harmony in the workplace, especially in response to Situation during and after the Kovid-19 crisis.
Please be reminded that in January 2018, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training signed a Memorandum of Understanding with ACILS on the implementation of policies related to the labor sector and workplace harmony for 3 years (Date January 22, 2018 to January 22, 2021). After the memorandum of understanding was finalized, the two sides signed a two-year cooperation agreement.
It should be noted that in the past, Cambodia has worked closely with the United States to implement trade linkages to working conditions. Through this cooperation, Cambodia has strived to strengthen the implementation of better working conditions that meet the concerns of all stakeholders. All, including major US buyers, unions, employers, workers. As a result, Cambodia still maintains the market and the prestige of goods made in Cambodia.
