19 Kovid patients fleeing, please immediately report to authorities if this person is found
(Phnom Penh): A 19-year-old Kovid patient escaped from the Chattalysak site on July 26, 2021. Authorities appealed to residents who saw the person with the disorder as shown in the picture to report immediately.
The 19 Kovid patients who escaped were named Soeung Vutha, a 24-year-old male resident of Tuol Roka 1 village, Chak Angre Krom commune, Meanchey district.
According to the Kovid 19 Research Subcommittee, Soeung Vutha was tested positive for Kovid 19 when he was admitted to Ang Duong Hospital on July 25, 2021.
Due to his surgery, Soeung Vutha was briefly admitted to Ang Duong Hospital before being transferred to Kovid Medical Center. Only on July 26, 2021, this person disappeared from Ang Duong Hospital and can not be contacted until now.
The escape is in violation of the 199 Kovid Fighting Act, which carries severe penalties and, if transmitted, can lead to imprisonment. Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin: Cambodia-China relations are at their best stage as China plays an important role in helping to build and develop in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin, Minister in Charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, emphasized that bilateral relations between Cambodia and China are at their best and have become a model of friendly living and close cooperation. .
In 2021, Cambodia and China have had diplomatic relations for 63 years. For the past 63 years, Cambodia-China relations have maintained close ties and worked closely together to overcome difficulties in bilateral, regional and international frameworks.
Today's forum aims to promote mutual understanding, to strengthen and expand the long-term friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and China, as well as to contribute to the joint efforts of the two governments. Both to strengthen and expand cooperation in the fields of politics, economy and socio-culture closer, especially the people-to-people relations of our two countries better.
Deputy Prime Minister Binh Minh highlighted in an online program in front of senior Cambodian and Chinese officials that Cambodia and China are two countries with a long history of traditional and friendly relations.
"Relations between the two countries are always based on respect for sovereignty and non-interference in each other's internal affairs and mutual respect," he added. "Cambodia has always adhered to the one-China policy and supported the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) policy and the establishment of the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank (AIIB) to connect countries across Asia."
"I believe that China has also been playing an important role in Cambodia's economic recovery during and after Kovid-19," said Binh Chin. "In terms of politics, economy, society and culture, Cambodia-China relations are at an unprecedented level in history."
In this morning's forum, Deputy Prime Minister Binh Chin also mentioned China's participation in the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia. The Deputy Prime Minister said that in the difficult situation that Cambodia is struggling with the Kovid-19 epidemic, China has actively helped Cambodia, both in terms of technical assistance, both material and vaccine, and has coordinated and given priority to Cambodia. Order more vaccines.
