(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, stated that China is not only an important trading partner of Cambodia, but also Cambodia and China are active and indispensable partners in policy formulation and trade negotiations. Regional and global.
The statement was made by the senior trade official on the sidelines of the 2nd Cambodia-China Brain Bank High-Level Forum: A New Phase in the Development of Cambodia-China Bilateral Trade Relations on July 28.
Mr. Sok Sopheak said: "Over the years, trade figures have clearly shown that China is an important trading partner of Cambodia. "Moreover, Cambodia and China are active and indispensable partners in policy formulation and trade negotiations, both within the framework of the World Trade Organization and at the regional level."
He said that the total trade between Cambodia and China is always beyond the plan set by the heads of government of the two countries. In fact, in 2017, total trade increased by 16% to 5.8 billion US dollars, exceeding the target. In 2020, as the two countries were affected by the 19-crisis Kuwait, growth slowed by 5 percent, but total bilateral trade remained large at more than $ 8 billion.
He stressed that at the regional level, the two countries have complemented each other well with the flexibility that has helped make negotiations successful. In fact, in December 2002, on the occasion of Cambodia hosting the ASEAN Summit, Cambodia facilitated the signing of the China-ASEAN Framework Agreement on Comprehensive Economic Cooperation, which paved the way for an agreement. ASEAN-China Free Trade in the coming years.
