Some officials and authorities of Kampong Thom province seized the tractor of the people in Stong district and demanded to pay $ 10,000 as a ransom for the tractor.
(Kampong Thom): Many people in some districts of Kampong Thom province reported that some professional officials often use the pretext of cracking down on crimes, accusing them of clearing state forest land or flooded forest. Seize their tractors to demand tens of thousands of dollars from them, which has caused a great deal of criticism, but no action has been taken yet.
According to some reports provided to Fresh News today, a number of officials and experts conspired with a group of journalists to seize tractors and machinery from people clearing land to extort money. Ten thousand dollars and then release the machine back.
In fact, on July 17, 2021, there was a case where the chief of Doung commune, Prasat Balang district reported on the force of forest chiefs, military officers and journalists who seized two tractors of people who cleared their fields in Ta Mom village, Doung commune. Prasat Balong district, they are required to pay a ransom of $ 8,000.
In Stong district, on July 26, 2021, a group of fisheries officials went to seize people's tractors, claiming that they had cleared community land and kidnapped them. Up to $ 10,000 will be released.
The seizure team, led by Meng in the fisheries department, also called the owner of the machine to demand a $ 10,000 ransom. Later, another mediator, Seiha, who was in the fisheries department, came out to negotiate with the owner of the equipment to facilitate the payment of the ransom, but the fishery was still stubborn in the amount of $ 10,000.
According to the report, the authorities and officers have a three-step scenario, including:
* First: At first, they asked a group of journalists who were their allies to go down and take pictures at the location where they could eat, threatening to publish the information in public and extort money from the owner of the field or the owner. Machinery according to the desired number.
* Second: If the first step is not achieved, they release the police force, police or fisheries chief, as described above, come down and confiscate the machinery and leave it at the district military command or forest office or administrative post. Etc. and continue to extort money from the people who own more machines, but in higher amounts than the first step, which can reach tens of thousands of dollars.
* Third: If the second step is still not completed, they will re-apply the law by sending the case to the prosecutor to carry out the procedure with the judiciary, and the money that the people have to give up is Many almost lost the blood of the farmers.
As for the mechanism of negotiating the payment, they let other people come to negotiate with the people. This is just a rough guide to the modern work of these officials. People who suffer because of this is not small in Kampong Thom province, or more precisely, is more common in Stong, Prasat Balong, Sandan, Prasat Sambo.
Residents of Prasat Balang district were also affected by the confiscation of their machinery by forest officials, who demanded $ 10,000 from him, but he could not afford to pay $ 7,000. Hungry for the money, he refused, and our people asked for $ 8,000. And they still do not agree.
In the district of Prasat Throne, there was also one of his family who was arrested by the forest chief and his grandfather was arrested. The old man's family also asked for mediation at the district level, but only solved the machine, while the old man was sent to detention for four days to prepare a case to send him to court.
To make matters worse, when the authorities take people's machinery and store it at their headquarters, it often disappears from the machinery as often as it can.
This heinous act is like destroying the achievements of the leaders who are always trying to build the people, especially the trust of the people who always trust the government through the ballot. Precious. Some district leaders also seem to be numb and do not pay much attention to the actions of these officials, which may lead to the loss of the ballot in the future.
