The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on July 23 issued a decision on the establishment of a sub-committee on law enforcement under the Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Fight against Kovid 19.
In this decision, the Sub-Committee on Law Enforcement is chaired by Mr. Thong Lim, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, accompanied by 3 Vice-Chairmen and 7 members.
The Sub-Committee on Law Enforcement has the following duties:
* Lead and coordinate the implementation of administrative measures, health measures and legal measures for the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19
* Introduce necessary measures to strengthen the implementation of measures related to the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19
* Monitor and monitor the implementation of measures, including health measures, administrative measures and legal measures that are put in place to prevent and control the spread of Kovid 19
Propose new measures or modifications to respond to the actual evolution of the situation of Kovid 19 epidemic to the CEC Executive Committee.
* Monitor and evaluate the progress of the implementation of measures related to the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 and make regular reports to the Executive Committee of CEC and
Perform other tasks as assigned by the Executive Committee of the CEC.
