The event was attended by Mr. Chiravudy Sovanart, General Business Adviser, accompanied by Thai Embassy officials representing the Thai Embassy and International Trade Promotion Office in Cambodia, as well as representatives of the Thai private sector in Cambodia.
The program of the Thai Embassy and the private sector in Cambodia aims to support the Royal Government of Cambodia in the care of Cambodian workers affected by the Kovid-19 epidemic, which is considered a key factor in promoting growth. Thai and Cambodian economies.
In addition, it demonstrates the Royal Government of Thailand's commitment to taking care of Cambodian workers living in Thailand as well as returning to Cambodia.
In the past, the Thai Embassy and the private sector in Cambodia have also jointly donated food and some supplies to Cambodian migrant workers at Chattalysak Center in Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey provinces.
