According to some reports, the smuggling of cigarettes into Vietnam through the Phnom Krahorm corridor in Pak Nhay commune, O'Yadao district, is still under scrutiny by the authorities and relevant institutions.
In fact, on July 24, 2021, a truck carrying cigarettes from a warehouse in Banlung traveled on National Road 78 and approached the O'Yadaw International Gate, turning right at the Vietnamese Rubber Company (74) and crossing into Vietnam through the Red Mountain Corridor. The smuggling of goods into Vietnam through such uncontrolled corridors carries a significant risk of contracting Kovid 19.
