(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Japan, Mr. Shugayoshi Hyde, has expressed his commitment to do his utmost to cooperate with Cambodia for the success of the Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) hosted by Cambodia.
In a message sent to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News on July 26, 2021, the Prime Minister of Japan stated: Importantly, as the chair of the meeting, I will cooperate to the best of my ability for the success of these meetings.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, expressed his eagerness to work closely with the Prime Minister of Japan in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks, especially on the occasion of the Asia-Europe Summit. To be hosted by video in November this year and on the occasion of Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN next year for the mutual benefit of the two nations and peoples.
Cambodia will host the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) on November 25-26, 2021, which will be televised due to the spread of Kovid 19, especially infectious diseases. In the community, February 20 has dragged on so far.
The 13th Asia-Europe Summit was attended by a total of 53 leaders from Asia and Europe, including 21 from Asia and 30 from Europe, as well as the ASEAN Secretariat. And the European Union.
The summit played an important role in promoting Asia-Europe partnership and cooperation to promote peace, economic prosperity and social progress. The summit is held every two years, taking turns to host one of the member states in Europe and again in Asia.
