(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on July 26, 2021 issued a notice telling mobile phone operators to stop harassing users by calling the following numbers.
The order comes after the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia (TCC) previously found that some mobile operators were using short codes or different numbers to call users to advertise. Advertising about its value-added services (VAS) by unregistered users, which disrupts daily life and goes against the will of the users.
In this regard, the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia has issued instructions to all mobile service providers as follows: The name is pre-used by the user.
2: Immediately stop the use of any telecommunications code without the permission of the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia.
The Ministry emphasizes that in case the mobile service providers do not follow the above instructions, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications will take strict action by instructing the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia to freeze all the requests of those operators and take action accordingly. Article 69 and Article 78 of the Law on Telecommunications.
