Vital Continues Campaign to Plant 1,000 Mangrove Trees for the Second Time in Prek Tnaot Fishing Community, Kampot Province
(Phnom Penh): Vital Drinking Water Company has brought about 20 employees together with Prek Tnaot fishing community and with the support of Kampot Provincial Department of Environment to organize a campaign to plant 1,000 mangrove trees in the protected area of Prek Tnaot fishing community in Kampot province. This morning, July 23, 2021.
This is the second time that Vital Drinking Water Company has organized a mangrove planting campaign in Kampot province in order to encourage the participation of the public everywhere, especially the private sector to participate in the maintenance and protection of mangrove forests, which are important habitats for biodiversity and An important resource that balances ecosystems and the environment.
On this occasion, Mr. Chun Heang Thav Sith, Vice President of Business of Vital Drinking Water Company, said that the mangrove forest not only provides great benefits for the environment and economy of the fishermen living in the surrounding area, but also acts as a barrier. Protects coastal storms and also provides shelter to diverse water resources, which are a major tourist attraction.
"Together, planting mangroves today demonstrates the united spirit of humanity to uplift the environment and create a wonderful memory of humanity's commitment to the environment," he said.
Mr. Dao Soth, Representative of the Director of the Department of Environment of Kampot Province, confirmed that the planting of mangrove trees today is an important contribution from private companies to help conserve mangrove forests and jointly maintain the environment.
He hopes that this activity will encourage and mobilize the contribution of the general public to continue to conserve mangrove forests in support of the Prek Tnaot fishing community, which is in need of our help.
It should also be noted that Vital Drinking Water Company has always participated in many social and charitable activities, such as planting trees, giving charitable gifts, sponsoring programs and organizing many other programs for society.
Vital is a local company that has received strong support from the Cambodian people for its philanthropic and social work for more than 10 years. The company also called on the public, young people and the private sector to understand the unique benefits of mangrove trees and continue to plant more mangrove trees and maintain the forest for the long-term benefit of the community. And the environment as a whole.
