The following is the press release of Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration: A family of Cambodian workers found out that they had crossed the Kovid 19 and decided to walk through the forest and risked to return home.
(Banteay Meanchey): A family of Cambodian workers, a couple and their three young sons and daughters, when they realized that they had crossed the Kovid 19, they decided to walk through the forest and risked to return home. Troop 51 was arrested at 10:00 AM on July 25, 2021 in front of Star Golf, Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Border guards told Fresh News on July 26, 2021 that when questioned, the wife replied that her family had crossed the forest and risked to return home from Thailand because they had fallen. He was sick and suspected of infecting Kovid 19.
They are traders in Rong Klue Market, Aranya District, Sa Kaeo Province, Thailand and reside in Poipet. Police confirmed that they went to Thailand through two brokers to help cross the border in the past, but the two suspects have also been arrested. He said that when he arrived in Thailand, his family became ill and could not stay in Thailand, so they were forced to cross the border into Cambodia on their own.
After questioning and taking notes, the five were sent by the 911th Border Guard Police and the 51st Military Division in military vehicles to be stationed at a location in Poipet City. Upon arrival at the center, the doctors performed a quick test and found a positive result. This is really lucky that the front line forces prevent in time to spread to others.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance announces the opening of a series of training courses on "Technical Skills in Public Financial Management 2021"
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of Monday, July 26, 2021, the Ministry of Economy and Finance opened a series of training courses on "Technical Skills on Public Financial Management 2021" for a total of 320 target trainees who are Ministry officials - Institution in charge of public financial management.
The opening ceremony of the online training course was held under the leadership of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and attended by the Under-Secretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance, Lead representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, trainers and trainees.
The Secretary of State further stressed that in the context of economic globalization, climate change, the threat of a global pandemic, along with the development of information technology, Cambodia needs to be well prepared in terms of capacity and resources to maintain Achieve the competitiveness and sustainability of past achievements in socio-economic development and to move towards economic recovery in the aftermath of the global epidemic of Kovid-19.
The Secretary of State stressed that public financial management reform is currently in the third and second phase, with the goal of "strengthening the linkage of budget to policy" and "completing the preparation towards accountability." In the next four phases, with the transfer of more ownership and responsibilities to all ministries and institutions.
At the same time, the Information Technology System for Public Financial Management (FMIS) has been implemented in all ministries and institutions to ensure the transparency, efficiency, consistency and timeliness of financial information, which is a necessary requirement of the management and civil servants of All ministries and institutions for effective and comprehensive implementation.
Mr. Hean Sahip emphasized that this makes the building and development of capacity more important because all ministries and institutions, both at the national level and at the sub-national administration, must participate in the implementation of the full program budget and budget units as tools and It is a key mechanism for achieving policy objectives in linking the budget to the priority policies of the Royal Government.
