Cambodian Deputy Foreign Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, said that Japan's continued assistance reflected strong bilateral ties (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) From the strong bilateral relations between the two countries.
This was stated by the Deputy Prime Minister at the signing ceremony of an exchange of letters on the Japanese grant to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the implementation of the "Human Resource Development Scholarship" project in 2021 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation. International of Cambodia this morning, July 26, 2021.
Through this project, 26 Cambodian government officials (of which 24 are pursuing a master's degree and 2 are pursuing a doctorate) will benefit from pursuing higher education in Japan.
Japan also recently announced the provision of 1 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine to the Royal Government of Cambodia, of which 33 million doses of the first vaccine were delivered to Cambodia on the 24th. July 2021.
In addition to these, Japan is also strongly supporting our efforts to combat Kovid-19 by providing more than $ 50 million in grants and about $ 230 million in loans.
Mr. Prak Sokhon added that on behalf of the Cambodian people, Samdech Techo expressed his deep gratitude to the Government of Japan and described the donation as "new evidence that reflects a deep humanitarian gesture and great responsibility." "Japan's support for countries with limited resources and capabilities in the fight against Kovid-19."
Cambodia and Japan formally established relations on January 9, 1953. Cambodia-Japan relations continued to improve until becoming a strategic partnership in December 2013. Trade and investment cooperation between the two countries has been continuously strengthened and expanded.
In 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and Japan was about $ 2 billion, of which Cambodia exported about 1.2 billion to Japan and Japan imported about 800 million. In the first nine months of 2020, the trade volume between the two countries is about 800 million dollars, of which Cambodia exports to Japan about 500 million dollars and Japan imports about 300 million dollars to Cambodia.
