(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has provided 362 million yen (approximately 3.3 million US dollars) in additional assistance to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the implementation of the "Human Resource Development Scholarship" project in 2021.
The signing ceremony of the letter on the exchange of Japanese grant funding took place this morning, July 26, 2021, at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia in the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs. And International Cooperation and Mr. MIKAMI Masahiro, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia.
He said that during the outbreak of Kovid-19, Japan's continued assistance to Cambodia reflected the strong bilateral relations between our two countries and Japan's continued support for Long-term development in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's message is in response to a message from the Prime Minister of Japan sent to Samdech with more than 330,000 doses of 1 million doses of vaccine delivered to Cambodia on the 24th. July 2021 ago.
In the message, the Japanese Prime Minister said that the spread of Kovid 19 virus has also affected the exchanges between our two countries, but the Japanese cooperation project in Cambodia has been going well. Strong. "I am also focusing on moving forward with important projects that are indispensable for Cambodia's economic development, such as the Sihanoukville Port and National Road 5 projects."
In addition to providing vaccine assistance, Japan has also assisted the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against the Kovid-19 pandemic by providing over US $ 50 million in grant financing and approximately US $ 230 million in concessional loans.
The Prime Minister looks forward to working closely with the Prime Minister of Japan in both bilateral and multilateral frameworks, especially on the occasion of the Asia-Europe Summit to be held via video in November. This year and on the occasion of Cambodia's chairmanship of ASEAN next year for the mutual benefit of our nation and people.
