At the same time, Mr. Sin Chanserivutha said that the airline has reduced the staff in all departments except the air traffic control, especially they have tried to find a market by switching from some passenger transport to freight.
According to Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, in the first 5 months of 2021, air transport in Cambodia decreased by 92% while freight transport moved slightly.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha stated that the increase in air transport was due to the increase in the use of many goods such as online goods and other goods, including the delivery of vaccines and medical equipment.
In addition, Mr. Sin Chanserivutha pointed out that in the first five months of 2021, Cambodia's three international airports received 115,353 passengers, equivalent to 4,134 feet, while transporting 22,973 tons.
According to a senior civil aviation official, air travel is projected to improve by 2023.
Please be informed that in order to help the tourism sector, the Royal Government has introduced a series of tax incentives. In fact, on June 29, 2021, the Royal Government decided to extend the Minimum Tax exemption for an additional three months from July to September 2021 to airlines registered in Cambodia.
At the same time, the Royal Government has extended the payment of civil aviation fees for an additional three months from July to September 2021, with the permission of these airlines to arrange the payment of such debts in the post-term period. This delay.
