The following is the press release of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration: General Knowledge: Where does the "alphabet" writing system that we use as we have today come from?
The use of the alphabetical writing system is the same as it is today, we just combine the letters, vowels and punctuation, it will form a syllable or word as needed, while the alphabet writing system requires users to Note the appearance of each letter, such as the letters in ancient Egypt.
In fact, the characters we use in English today are rooted in the Sanskrit or Phoenician alphabet, but from generation to generation there have been changes in the appearance of some of the characters in order to make them easier to remember and study. Easy to write only.
Subsequent civilizations, including Indian, Greek, Roman, French, English, as well as our Khmer civilizations, all used the same alphabetical writing system, only the language had a different sound and each character had its own shape. Only different.
