(Siem Reap): More than 300 families in Peam Ta Uor village are participating in a campaign to collect plastic waste from the Tonle Sap Lake before the rainy season. The work was carried out in collaboration with the Tampaing Snong Russey Foundation and the authorities of Keo Por commune, Puok district.
According to a press release from Vine, the campaign starts on July 15 and is scheduled to end on July 30.
"Due to the current epidemic of Kovid 19 in the community, we are unable to hold this year's Tonle Sap Water Festival this year, which is an annual plastic waste collection campaign," the statement said. Before the Tonle Sap floods came back. "But this does not mean that flooded communities in the area around the Tonle Sap Lake can not collect plastic in their communities."
Sea Sophea Bamboo President Sa Sophal said that the community will collect the plastic waste left over and left over when the water recedes so that it does not flow back into the lake because when the water rises, if we do not collect It will absorb those plastic wastes that could seriously affect the ecosystem and pollute the biodiversity of the Tonle Sap Lake.
Mr. Sea Sophal expects that Peam Ta Uor villagers will collect about 3,000 bags of garbage during the water festival that will start soon. He added that in November 2020, the villagers collected about 2,000 bags of plastic garbage during the Water Festival.
