(Phnom Penh): The specialized force of the Anti-Drug Officers of the General Commission of the National Police launched an operation to crack down on criminals processing, storing, transporting and trafficking drugs in one case, arresting 5 suspects, including 4 Vietnamese and 4 Cambodians. One person and a total of 156 kilograms of drugs were seized.
