A farmer family in Preah Vihear province's Chep district succeeds in growing all kinds of vegetables in one year, earning more than 20 million riels
Soy Bopha, a farmer, described this morning, July 24, 2021, that she and her family had been growing vegetables for more than 10 years. The vegetables he grows include: cucumber, eggplant, watermelon and many other leafy vegetables on 2 hectares of land.
The farmer stated that the period of growing her vegetables in the first few years was not as successful as expected, due to the lack of technical conditions, lack of equipment ... etc. As a result, selling his vegetables a day can earn more than 50,000 riels.
Since 2018, with the support of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province, both materials and techniques have made his vegetable growing career very successful, earning 15,000 Riels per day. In general, he can earn more than 40 million riels a year, but he can still have more than 20 million riels left to pay for materials and labor.
The farmer thanked the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries for always supporting her vegetable growing career. Without this support, she would not have been as successful as she is today.
The farmer also appealed to people who have vacant land, if you want to grow vegetables, please contact him for information, he will help train you to grow without pay.
