(Phnom Penh): The Supreme Court of Cambodia recently decided to dissolve three other political parties that have been inactive in their activities and reports for many years after a complaint from the Ministry of Interior.
According to the Supreme Court ruling, which was received by Fresh News, the three long-inactive parties include Hor Mengheang's Khmer Democratic Party, which was dissolved on July 12, 2021, the Khemarak Moha Party. The kingdom of Mr. Phan Sina, who was sentenced to dissolve on July 12, 2021 and the Social Democrat Party of Mr. Thong Sovannara, who was sentenced to dissolve on July 12, 2021.
General Khieu Sopheak, a spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, confirmed to Fresh News that the Ministry of Interior had filed a complaint with the Supreme Court after the three parties had been silent and inactive for many years. Contactable.
Since 2017, about four political parties have been dissolved by the court for serious violations and inaction. However, so far in Cambodia, about 50 other parties are active, some of which have already announced their readiness to run in the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council elections and elections. Parliamentary elections in 2023.
According to Khieu Sopheak, many new parties are now being formed and have applied to the Ministry of Interior.
