The following is the announcement of Prey Veng Provincial Administration: KOICA will provide online training on "Administrative Capacity Building on Women's Policy"
(Phnom Penh): The KOICA office in Cambodia will provide training to 20 Cambodian government officials from the Ministry of Women's Affairs of Cambodia on "Administrative Capacity Building on Women's Policy." The training will be held online from July 26 to August 4, 2021 for 10 days.
KOICA has resumed its online training, considering that it will be difficult to implement a direct training program in Korea in 2021 due to the Kovid-19 epidemic.
Objectives of the training online or online: First, to enhance the capacity building of the administration on the protection of women's rights and gender equality; Second, to establish the basis for expanding the scope of activities of global gender policy professionals through Share experiences of women's policy development; and third, create a gender-equitable society by promoting social participation, work, work-life balance, safety and health for women.
During this 10-day online training, participants will learn about 1: Identifying current problems by studying the report 2: Finding solutions through learning, discussion through Online, etc. And 3: Present the action plan at the last workshop.
KOICA will continue to support and implement programs in Cambodia that focus on human resource development. From 1994 to 2020, KOICA invited about 3,100 government officials to participate in short-term training and master's programs in the Republic of Korea under the KOICA-KOICA Capacity Building Program. Ministry of Interior Informs National Heart Party to Amend Statute and Complete Files 15 Days Before Re-Registration
