Accounting and Auditing Regulators Disseminate Accounting and Auditing Obligations and Related Provisions for Nonprofits
(Phnom Penh): The Accounting and Auditing Regulator has organized an outreach workshop on "Accounting and Auditing Obligations and Related Provisions" for Nonprofits.
This workshop was held on the morning of Thursday, July 13, 2021, under the chairmanship of Mr. Butharin, Director General of Accounting and Regulatory Affairs. The audit will be attended by the management and officials of the accounting and auditing regulators and about 250 participants in the Zoom program.
Mr. Bou Tharin highlighted the importance and importance of the workshop for nonprofits to increase awareness of the obligations that nonprofits must perform in accordance with applicable laws and regulations related to accounting and auditing. .
He mentioned the main obligations that non-profit organizations have to perform, including 1) the obligation to keep the accounts, 2) the obligation to prepare financial statements in accordance with the applicable standards and 3) the obligation to submit financial statements. Independent audit.
Following the opening remarks of the Director General and the presentation by the Technical Officer, the participants inquired about the use of language and currency in the preparation of accounting records and the preparation of the annual financial statements, as well as the submission of financial statements for audit. Accounting and Auditing Regulators.
It should also be noted that non-profit organizations that properly perform these obligations will have many benefits, such as transparency in the management of financial resources, increased trust from donors, and greater access to funding. The effectiveness of the use of funds and services to help the society and the avoidance of punishment from the authorities.
