National Bank of Cambodia: The banking and financial system remains resilient and provides sustainable financial services
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, spoke about the resilience of the banking sector during the outbreak of Kovid 19, in which the banking system, banking and financial institutions continue to be resilient and provide financial services. Sustainable stuff to customers.
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks were made at the organizing ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of the first half and the work direction of the second half of 2021 of the National Bank of Cambodia on July 22, 2021.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Royal Government has taken drastic measures to control the spread of Kovid 19 with increasing vaccination and Fast.
He said the capital situation was also strong, with a transparency ratio of 24.4% for the banking sector and 22.7% for the microfinance sector, a high liquidity of 159.8% for banking institutions and 175.6%. For deposit-taking microfinance institutions.
At the same time, he said, the non-performing loan ratio was low at 2.4% for the banking sector and 2% for the microfinance sector, while banking and financial institutions were also allowed to restructure loans to alleviate the burden on the people. Affected.
In addition, to alleviate the burden on the affected people, the banking and financial institutions have reorganized 367,239 loans, equivalent to 22.2 trillion riels (US $ 5.5 billion).
In line with the advancement of technology, the National Bank of Cambodia has strengthened the development of payment systems based on new financial technologies such as QR code payments, remittances and mobile payments. Among them, the Bakong system, which uses blockchain technology, has been introduced and is a payment system for payments through banking and financial institutions, as well as various payments.
All of these payment systems are actively involved in supporting business, trade and investment activities. In order to continue to support socio-economic stability and economic recovery, the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to implement measures to support growth and contribute to maintaining strong macroeconomic and financial stability in line with government policies.
