The Ministry of Posts found that Smart followed the wrong procedure to open a phone number for customers and cut off the number from customers who are using it to sell to others.
This is according to the press release on the action against misconduct in opening the telephone number of customers of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, which Fresh News received on the afternoon of July 22, 2021.
In this statement, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications said that in order to protect the rights and interests of mobile phone users, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications would like to inform the public about the action taken against Smart Asiata Co., Ltd. as follows:
* First: Smart Asiata Co., Ltd. must make a public apology by posting on its official website and promising not to let the above incident happen again.
* Second: Smart Asiata Co., Ltd. must provide compensation to the original owner for misconduct in closing the phone number from the customer who is using.
* Fourth: All individuals involved in the above cases will be held accountable before the law in force.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications also reminded all mobile service providers to strengthen the management and procedures for the proper distribution and sale of mobile phone SIM cards to their customers to avoid such incidents. The Ministry will continue to monitor and take the strictest action in accordance with the laws and regulations in force for mobile phone service providers who have committed wrongdoing.
