(Pailin): Farmers living along the Cambodian-Thai border, especially in Pailin province, have begun to harvest a series of red corn crops, with market prices seemingly slightly higher than last year. According to farmers' claims.
In fact, on July 22, 2021, some farmers who were harvesting red corn said that they were suffering from unfavorable natural disasters, causing their crops to suffer forever, such as lice and earthworms. Due to the continuous daily rain, it caused waterlogging in the corn fields, causing severe damage to the corn crop and then drying up, causing a lot of loss of yield.
Ms. But Srey Oun, a farmer in Koun Phnom village, Otavao commune, Pailin city, said that this year she really lost a lot of money by buying corn seeds to plant on 4 hectares of land, hoping that when the harvest can Will sell some money to pay off debts and the rest to support daily life. But due to the natural disaster, the heavy rain made him very desperate and could not seem to find the money to pay off his debts.
The red corn crop in 2021 will not be as productive as last year because when the corn is growing, red spiders and swarms of worms come to destroy it, and this year, the rainfall is irregular, that is, when it rains. Every day, it causes rot, sometimes it dries, causing it to wither, so it is not very effective. Due to this reason, this year, almost everyone who grows corn complains.
As for the market price, 1 kg of red corn, traders buy 5.2 baht (Thai currency) equal to more than 600 riel per kilogram, which is slightly higher than last year. General knowledge: Get to know the man who has the most wives
(World): In today's society, there is usually only one husband and one wife in a family, but for an Indian man, he has dozens of wives, while many sources consider him a married man. Most in the world.
At one time, he married up to 10 wives a year. Jana married his 39th wife in 2004 at the age of 25. His large family lives in a large, four-story house with a total of 100 rooms, and all of his wives live in a large shared room next to his own room.
Of course, the law in India does not allow for polygamy or polygamy, but Indian authorities in some states, especially in the northeast, allow some tribes or religious sects to adhere to this tradition. Their customs.
However, Ziona Chana just passed away in June 2021 at the age of 76, leaving one of the largest families in the world.
