(Phnom Penh): The new president of the Cambodian Hotel Association (CHA), Mr. Din Somethearith, said that the association has been seeking financial assistance from the Royal Government to help save the business of its members affected by the Kovid-19 crisis. The hotel sector in Cambodia is still in a very difficult situation, with some hotels closing down, others holding back, despite heavy losses, and others almost bankrupt.
In an interview with Fresh News at the end of July, Mr. Din Somethearith said that the hotel sector in Cambodia is completely dependent on the aviation sector, which is a way to bring foreign tourists to visit Cambodia and accept accommodation services in Cambodia. Cambodia. When flights were restricted during the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as the need for a catastrophe, the hotel business was in crisis.
The president of the hotel association said that according to the latest report he received, about 50 hotels were permanently closed, while some were open only on weekends, sometimes with fewer guests. There are no guests, and some hotels have a restaurant, so most business owners close the hotel but still open some restaurants.
The Cambodian Hotel Association has been looking for solutions in every way to keep the hotel business alive and thriving, he said. With representatives of relevant partners on a financial project that will release a second budget loan package for small and medium enterprises (SMEs) without the need for collateral.
At this point, Mr. Din Somethearith would like to emphasize that "All business owners in the hotel industry can also apply for this budget loan package to continue to survive and save their business, as this loan package is up to 300,000. The dollar, and when the government decides to approve, the association will publish to its members. He hopes that the government will continue to provide more assistance to the hotel sector.
On behalf of the new President of the Cambodian Hotel Association, Mr. Din Somethearith appealed to business owners in the hotel, guesthouse or other accommodation business owners who have not yet joined the Cambodian Hotel Association to join as many members as possible to help solve the problem. Issues in its field to contribute to the Royal Government in maintaining the stability of the hotel sector and continue to grow.
