The Minister of Health delivered a speech on "ASEAN Response to Kovid-19 after 1 Year" with the following contents:
Cambodia successfully managed to respond to the Kovid-19 pandemic throughout 2020, with fewer than 500 positive cases and no deaths. Cambodia is very proud of the great efforts of the whole society, this remarkable achievement occurs under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In response to the February 20, 2021 community event, Cambodia has updated the structure of the National Kovid-19 Commission, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. The revised structure includes the participation of all sectors in the management, coordination, response to the 19 cases of Kovid under the Standing Committee of the National Committee for Kovid-19.
In addition, four commissions have played important roles in supporting the 19 response to Kovid, including: 1. The Intergovernmental Commission for the Fight against Kovid-19, which manages 102 sub-committees; Procurement of Kovid vaccine 193: Commission for vaccination of Kovid 19 Nationwide framework 4: 25 Kovid vaccination commission 19 Capital-Province.
This requires the introduction of a number of "health approaches beyond health and innovative investments" for future investment. With the discovery of the new Delaware and Alpha Kovid-19 virus, the Prime Minister has set out six strategies:
1: Continue to prevent the import of new mutant viruses 2: Reduce the size of the infected area and infected areas 3: Strive for early treatment 4: Search and control 5: Organize and manage corpses and 6: Vaccination campaign
Pursuant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Flowering Strategy, the Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign has been actively pursuing the goal of vaccinating 10 million people aged 18 and over by June. 2022. With the current rate of vaccinations, we hope that the vaccination of 10 million target people will be completed within seven to eight months ahead of the master plan deadline.
The first priority groups to be vaccinated are frontline health workers, local authorities, the elderly and other vulnerable groups, as well as foreigners living in Cambodia. As of today, with the combined efforts of the Royal Government, health officials, volunteer doctors and military doctors, as well as local authorities, 65% of the 10 million target population have received at least one Kovid-19 vaccine. Dosage.
