16 unexploded ordnances were collected and burned by Kampong Tralach District Police in cooperation with CMAC
(Kampong Chhnang): 16 unexploded ordnance left over from the war were collected and burned by CMAC in cooperation with Kampong Tralach District Police Inspectorate in Kampong Chhnang Province on the morning of July 20. This year 2021.
Kampong Tralach district police said that the unexploded ordnance collected and burned above was old bullets left over from the war scattered in the fields and villages of the people, such as 82 mm bullets. 2 bullets, 4 M79 mm bullets, 6 60mm bullets, 1 105mm bullet and 3 107mm bullets.
According to the police, all the unexploded ordnance was found by the villagers in Sre Chamkar village, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province. They reported to the police and CMAC officials to collect and burn to avoid There is danger to the people in any way.
At the same time, officials of the Mine Action Center have appealed to the people if they find unexploded ordnance, no matter where it is, do not touch it to avoid any accident caused by unexploded ordnance. Explosion. Must immediately report to local police officers to cooperate with the CMAC Center to collect and burn.
