The handover ceremony of the distance learning system as well as the meeting and financial support and other items for the former teachers were held on July 21, 2021 at Tuol Tum Poung High School, Phnom Penh. The ceremony was organized in accordance with the health measures and instructions of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, "3 do not and 3 protection" and rapid test (Rapid Test).
Alumni of 1989 to become President of the Electricity Authority of Cambodia, Mr. Yim Viseth confirmed that he and the alumni of 1989 today can not be separated from the precious merits of the Cambodian People's Party with Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the party president and prime minister of Cambodia, and this project "is the first sponsorship project that the 1989 alumni have done and will certainly have more projects."
Alumni of Toul Tompong School, established in 1989, have clear goals, including:
* First: Take care of the former teachers who are now retired, sick and old, so it is important that we, as alumni, take care of them, that we can support them to a certain extent. During the national holidays and when he is very sick, we can help him as much as we can.
At the same time, he considered that the merit of the teacher is like the second parent, which is invaluable, so starting from school and the teacher made the group of students of Tuol Tompong High School in 1989 organize a gathering. Express gratitude to teachers and fundraising and hand over the current distance learning system to the school. In addition, this activity is also a good example for the next generation of students to emulate.
"Because Cambodia and the world are currently facing an epidemic of Kovid 19, so we have a plan to help the school, so we discussed it in our group," said the alumni representative. Including discussions with former retired teachers, including the principal, and he also proposed that this distance learning system is necessary ....! It is necessary to have this remote teaching system with a computer camera ...! "
On the other hand, Nuth Somalin, a former vocational teacher, was very happy for the 1989 alumni who organized two distance learning initiatives for Tuol Tompong High School and provided some financial support to the former teachers. Retired now
The former teacher assessed that the spirit of this group of alumni of the 1989 generation was to create big plans to help develop the school better. While the distance learning equipment is very helpful to the school as well as provide easy opportunities for students who have to prepare for the lower secondary school diploma (diploma) and high school graduation exam (Bakdup), etc.
Mr. Nguon Chanrithy, a former Khmer language teacher, spoke and supported the mindset of 1989 alumni and all generations of alumni who joined hands to donate, no matter how small, for our alumni school and to show solidarity. As a whole for the unity of society as well as to participate in the development of our school to be a light to prosperity.
