Cambodia-China Friendship Association Celebrates 63 Years of Cambodia-China Diplomatic Relations
Diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China were established by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and former Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China Zhou Enlai.
The strong ties between Cambodia and China have been demonstrated through frequent exchanges of visits between the two countries' top leaders. China has always regarded Cambodia-China bilateral relations as a steel relationship that no one can break. Official Cambodia-China relations were established on July 19, 1958, five years after Cambodia gained independence from France.
Over the past 63 years, the traditional friendship between Cambodia and China, pioneered by the previous generation of leaders and carefully cared for by the next generation of leaders of Cambodia and China, has been widely promoted. Constantly.
The two sides have maintained close cooperation in all fields, including politics, economy, trade, culture, humanity, as well as regional and international affairs, with great achievements. BREAKING: CDC: "All vaccines, even if fully administered, do not provide 100% protection against Kovid 19 infection"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has decided to reject the request of truck owners not to allow them to be overweight and continue to detain vehicles for one year for vehicles that are overweight. 20 percent or more.
On July 20, 2021, the owners of trucks transporting soil, sand and stones gathered to protest, asking the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to ease some conditions on their transportation. There are three proposals, including:
First, request to increase the weight or transport overweight between 9 tons to 15 tons, depending on the type of heavy truck in addition to the weight specified in the law; Weight over 20% up to 3: Request for the car to be returned to the owner of the company or car owner, just fine and do not need to detain the car again.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) stated that the above three points could not be resolved as requested, as they were contrary to the provisions of Articles 2 and 60 of the Law on Roads and Legal Documents in force. .
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has advised that transport company owners, truck owners or truck drivers should work together to implement legal measures to ensure the protection of public property, roads, bridges and road construction. Sturdy according to the technical life, determined in accordance with the standard level of construction.
Please be reminded that on July 20, 2021, yesterday, the owner of the truck and the driver of the truck gathered to protest at the location of the second ring road on the border of Phnom Penh-Kandal province with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport after the arrest. Stop their overweight car and keep it for a year.
With this protest, Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Overweight Transport Inspection Committee, led the delegation and the Standing Coordinating Committee to address and review the requests of the representatives of the transport vehicles. On the issue of overweight shipping as well.
Senior officials of the Ministry of Public Works instructed the owner of a sand depot in Takhmao City on the law on transportation to avoid transporting damaged roads
(Central): Mr. Kim San, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on July 21, 2021, led a working group to educate sand depot owners in Takhmao City on the Law on Mineral Transport in order to participate. Comply with technical standards on transportation to avoid overloading and damage to national roads.
Also present on this occasion were Mr. Uy Sambath, Deputy Director of the Secretariat of the Ministry of Public Works, Mr. Chuor Chhun Leng, Deputy Director of Kandal Provincial Public Works Department, Mr. Ming Youleng, Mr. Phin Madonna, Deputy Governor of Takhmao City and many other officials. Also.
Mr. Kimsan said that the visit to educate the depot owners is a soft education to strengthen the knowledge around traffic laws, especially focusing on fines for overweight and advise depot owners to continue to promote From this law to all sand-land transport drivers to clearly understand and abide by the stated law to avoid confusion and demand to be overweight.
He also claimed that the request of the sand-transporters yesterday was difficult to accept because according to a study by experts on road pressure, overloading was the main cause of damage. National roads.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that the working group will handle the procedure without understanding anyone if it is found that the trucks dare to carry overweight. The operation will continue throughout Kandal province and across the country to restrict transportation in accordance with the law to prevent criminals from arbitrarily destroying roads.
Another 1 million doses of Sinofam vaccine to arrive in Cambodia tomorrow morning
(Phnom Penh): An additional 1 million doses of Chinese Sinofam vaccine will arrive in Cambodia on the morning of Thursday, July 22, 2021 tomorrow.
Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, confirmed that the Sinofam vaccine that arrived in Cambodia tomorrow is an order of the Royal Government.
So far, Cambodia has received a total of 16 million doses of the vaccine. Of that, about 15.7 million doses are vaccines donated and purchased from China.
China has become an important country in helping Cambodia achieve this plan. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced that China is a strategic reference in the supply of vaccines.
As of July 20, Cambodia has already vaccinated more than 6 million people, which is about 62.02% of the target of 10 million people.
Cambodians are all aware of the value of vaccines in helping their health to fight Kovid 19. Those who have been vaccinated have expressed their happiness and deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for seeking to provide the vaccine to the Cambodian people for free. Ministry of Economy Meeting to Discuss Draft Framework and Roadmap on Cost Survey on Wastewater Infrastructure in Cambodia
The meeting was held on July 21, 2021 with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries and institutions of the Royal Government, members and members of the Sub-Committee on Exploration.
To begin with, the Minister stated that today's meeting is to discuss the draft framework and road map on costing on wastewater infrastructure in Cambodia and to collect inputs both in form and content. In accordance with both international practice and the actual situation in Cambodia.
During the discussion, Minister Vongsey Visoth said that the current demand for wastewater infrastructure in Cambodia has increased significantly, as well as other public infrastructure sub-sectors, while the Royal Government's financial resources for investment in this sector. Limited yet.
It has become increasingly challenging for the government to finance investment in wastewater infrastructure to meet the needs of better sanitation, address environmental issues, and respond to the city's rapid growth and development. And towns.
In principle, in deciding on an investment project in any city, the Ministry of Economy and Finance pays high attention not only to the source of funding and the estimated cost, but also focuses on the master plan, plan. Development and investment planning of the city, and especially the sustainability of these works, as well as institutional development, as their size increases and becomes more complex.
The Minister added that for the wastewater infrastructure project, there must be a clear plan and financing mechanism and cost quotation to ensure the cost-effectiveness and sustainability of the project.
To address these issues, the Sub-Committee on Costs is responsible for developing a cost-benefit framework and financing for wastewater infrastructure as a guideline for decision-making on future public investment projects to ensure economic and financial efficiency. And society and is sustainable within both the national and sub-national administrative frameworks.
