(Phnom Penh): As of 2021, Cambodia has received low-interest loans from the Government of the People's Republic of China for the construction of infrastructure worth a total of 2.865 million US dollars. This amount is equivalent to 90% of the money that Cambodia borrowed from China for the development of the country.
Of the $ 2.865 million in infrastructure loans, the Ministry of Public Works has completed the construction of 29 roads, equivalent to 2,888 km, and the construction of eight bridges with a total length of 8 km. $ 2.513 million. At the same time, the Ministry of Public Works is also building National Road No. 71C, National Road No. 10 at a cost of $ 322 million and Phnom Penh Port at a cost of $ 30 million.
In addition to the construction of the bridge, China has provided several low-interest loans for the construction of 29 roads, one Phnom Penh port, as well as the expansion of two national roads.
The presence of these roads and bridges has contributed to attracting more investors to develop in Cambodia from year to year. Rich infrastructure has helped factories move away from the city and closer to people in remote areas. In line with the slogan "There are roads, there are bridges, there is hope" by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Cambodia's economy has changed dramatically as roads and bridges have been extended to remote areas of agricultural and handicraft sources, as well as access to Cambodia to neighboring countries. This is a positive point that leads to the spread of the national economy to rural areas resulting from the policy of developing road and bridge infrastructure.
As the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highly valued China's assistance in the construction of roads and bridges in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo, the Prime Minister, once said, "All these points, if there is no China, ask who is really helping us, because others have only shouted and disciplined, but they have not given us anything." So, the question is, if we do not have good relations with China, can China afford to pay for our construction? "So I really understand that it is not wrong for us to pursue a partnership policy in cooperation with China."
