(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly, Chairman of the Council for Agriculture and Rural Development and Chairman of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition, this morning, July 21, 2021, led the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition. 10th video zoom system.
The 10th meeting of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition today has two main objectives: First, to review the progress report of the National Dialogue on the Food System and the direction for further implementation, and second: to review On the draft roadmap on sustainable food systems in Cambodia towards 2030.
The Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation have appointed Mr. Sok Silo, Secretary General of the CNCC. Convene national dialogues in coordination with relevant ministries and institutions, sub-national administrations, civil society development partners, the private sector, researchers and youth groups to gather input for the development of a roadmap on sustainable food systems in Cambodia. .
At the same time, the role of the National Dialogue is to be Cambodia's focal point in liaising with the Special Representative of the Secretary-General in charge of the organization of UN summits on the food system.
These documents will also be launched in Cambodia to increase stakeholders' awareness of the food system and to collaborate on their respective roles and responsibilities to make the food system stronger and more equitable. Finally, push forward the implementation of the Sustainable Development Goals by 2030.
