(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce on July 20, 2021 issued a press release explaining the role of the Ministry of Commerce on market prices and export-import goods, especially the price of imported pork. Prices in the domestic market and prices in neighboring countries Cambodia.
The Ministry of Commerce's statement came after a number of misconceptions regarding the role of the Ministry of Commerce on market prices and export-import goods, especially pork prices. Import.
The Ministry of Commerce said that since some public opinion does not reflect the role and duties of the Ministry of Commerce defined by the Constitution and the legal documents in force, the Ministry of Commerce would like to clarify to the public and the people as follows:
* Fifth, for the regular index of commodity prices in the Cambodian market, the Ministry of Commerce has the duty to cooperate with sub-national authorities only to collect general commodity indexes to be used as statistics for research, analysis and monitoring of inflation to set measures. Which can facilitate the flow of goods in the country and export-import through the free market mechanism only.
* Sixth: Regarding the request for a mechanism for extracting and coordinating the quantity and price of any strategic goods in the market, the Ministry of Commerce will cooperate with the relevant ministries and institutions to request a meeting under the framework of the committee. Economic and financial policy before respecting the request for high guidance from the head of the Royal Government on this issue.
