The Ministry also reminded the private sector tourists and the local management to pay attention to the implementation of the adventure tourism standard that the Ministry of Tourism introduced in 2015 to promote the organization of adventure tourism sites to comply with the standard to ensure Security - Safety for tourists.
According to the Ministry of Tourism, the main adventure tourism areas such as the back of Phnom Oral Kirirom Market, Chi Phat Areng area, Peam Krasop, Sre Ambel, Veal Thom, Samlot, Phnom Tbeng, Samuth Cheu, Reamsa, Tonle Sap Lake, Phnom Kulen and many more adventurous tourist sites Notable domestic tourism during the Kovid-19 crisis in 2020 and 2021.
In this sense, all adventure tourism sites must be organized to manage the flow of tourists, especially to make a clear tourist information before starting to enter the adventure area. Area managers must also monitor and instruct tourists to comply with the rules and restrictions set in each area, as well as to strengthen the implementation of tourism safety measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially Implement 3 measures and 3 protections.
At the same time, properly arrange bathrooms and toilets of appropriate size that can be arranged to ensure the beauty and reduce the impact on the environment and the tour of guests, as well as remind tourists to take care Environment and sustainable conservation of natural resources.
It should be noted that this adventure tourism standard is divided into 7 indicators as follows:
The World Tourism Organization (WTO) also considers ecotourism, adventure tourism, including rural tourism, as a sub-sector of world tourism that remains active and operational even during the Kovid-19 crisis, especially supporting domestic tourism activities and as a tool. Effective in promoting local development.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth Appreciates Kantha Bopha Hospital's Efforts to Examine and Treat Many Children in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Board of Trustees of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, praised Kantha Bopha Hospital for its efforts to examine and treat many children. In Cambodia.
Highly appreciated by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth during the online meeting of the Board of Governors of the "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" with the participation of Prof. Dr. Mam Ponheng, Minister of Health and members of the Board of Governors. To review and discuss the progress of the fund and the process of providing financial support to ensure the sustainability of the operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital.
The Deputy Prime Minister praised the efforts of Kantha Bopha Hospital to examine and treat a large number of children and encouraged them to continue this important work to contribute to the construction and development of bamboo shoots. Nation.
He praised the past efforts to mobilize donations and instructed the Secretariat to make more efforts to raise awareness of the presence and importance of the "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" for the purpose of fundraising. More from all walks of life to continue to contribute to support the operation and sustainability of Kantha Bopha Hospital and promote the spirit of "Khmer help Khmer" more widely.
"Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" has achieved significant results, including:
1: Progress of receiving donations and financial statements
2: Outreach activities and directions to raise donations
Due to the spread of Kovid 19, the Secretariat of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia has continued to focus on the practice of mobilizing online donations for the purpose of fundraising as well as publicizing the fund, with the following activities:
* Collaboration with partner financial institutions to receive donations in the form of e-donations,. * Production of a variety of promotional videos. Companies to advertise and collect donations. * Continuing to place donation boxes in public places, especially supermarkets and restaurants.
In addition to the progress and work direction of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia, the Board of Governors also received reports on the status of the five locations of Kantha Bopha Hospital for the first six months of 2021, in which the hospital received more than 226,194 patients. A total of 4,575 people were seriously ill and 10,190 underwent surgery.
The maternity ward of Kantha Bopha Siem Reap Hospital or Jayavarman VII Hospital examined and treated 41,855 pregnant women and gave birth to 10,323 children.
In addition, to help prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the hospital has set up a staff and staff structure to treat patients who have been diagnosed with Kovid 19 in a separate building from Hospitals in both Phnom Penh and Siem Reap.
