According to Fresh News on July 20, 2021, Mr. Pen Sovichet, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, claimed that the increase in oil prices was due to the increase in world oil prices. Expensive and in high demand.
A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce said that Cambodia is not an oil-producing country, it still buys refined oil from Singapore and other sources, and the oil it buys is based on price fluctuations. International crude oil.
"International crude oil prices have been rising for some time, especially in June and July," Pen Sovichet said.
According to a senior Commerce Ministry official, the rise in oil prices was due to OPEC cutting production and two major sources of crude oil exports: Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates. Has also reduced its oil production.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat said that the major countries in the OPEC region recently agreed to increase their oil production in August at 400,000 barrels per day, so oil will start. Rich again.
A senior Commerce Ministry official expects that in the near future, after the increase in oil production of major countries in the OPEC region, crude oil prices may fall in the international market, which is why Let the refined oil be reduced as well.
