(Phnom Penh): On July 21, 1979, 43 years ago, General Sao Sokha had the role of "Nasar, Commander of Unit 578", but because he was a person who had a good work for the service of his motherland. He was also given a series of roles before becoming the Commander of the National Gendarmerie. This is the writing of Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Gendarmerie on July 20, 2021.
Brigadier General Eng Hee wrote an article that read:
Tomorrow, from July 21, 1978 to the present, in 2021, multiplication and subtraction equals 43 years. Indeed, for 43 years, at that time, he served as the Commander of Unit 578. Later, due to the performance of duties, responsibilities, honesty, accomplishment of major tasks, was subsequently appointed to positions and was assigned to training. In Vietnam to the Soviet Union in political science and public administration.
He was the director of the Department of Youth in the Army, the Commissioner of Political Affairs of the Cambodian People's Revolutionary Army from 1983 to 1989. And from 1991 to 1993, he was assigned an important position to work with foreigners to participate in the implementation of the Paris Agreement on Cambodia: the position of chairman of the Joint Military Group of the State of Cambodia in Kampong Thom.
From 1993 to 1999, he was the Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and was appointed Commander-in-Chief of the National Gendarmerie to the present, His Excellency General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and a member of the Standing Committee. Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party.
