(Phnom Penh): The Department of Information Technology of the Ministry of Interior on July 20, 2021 presented a method to counter the tricks of the perpetrators of cybercrime, which is generally used by criminals to lure victims using financial means. Objects, materials, honors, or gifts of value.
The Department of Information Technology of the Ministry of Interior confirmed that its technical team has observed online and received a series of reports from citizens about new and different cyber crimes and some other types of crimes. That has happened before.
The technical team of the Department of Information Technology also shares a number of methods to support the general public to prevent and prevent themselves from becoming victims of cyber fraud.
The technical team of the Department of Information Technology has mentioned some programs that are common tricks of fraudsters for any malicious purpose, including:
* Perpetrators often lure victims by using methods that offer financial benefits, material honors, or gifts that are valuable and easy to obtain with easy terms.
* Use intimidation to intimidate victims in exchange for money or valuables.
In addition, the Department of Information Technology of the Ministry of Interior has presented four basic methods of self-defense as follows: 1: Be careful to buy goods or services that are cheaper than the market, because it may be counterfeit goods or tricks. Drag money laundering.
2: Consider and seek advice before giving money or valuables in various forms of investment that you do not know, do not understand the risks of investing.
3. Do not allow yourself to fall into the trap of intimidation or threats by crooks by consulting with your trusted friends or competent authorities before making any decisions.
4: Report to the competent authority or local authority where you live if you meet or find suspicion of fraud as mentioned above.
