Commentary: Sino-Cambodian friendship for 63 years "inseparable steel friend"
(Phnom Penh): China and Cambodia are friendly neighbors, the two countries have a long-standing traditional friendship. On July 19, 1958, China and Cambodia established formal diplomatic relations. Over the past 63 years, the Sino-Cambodian friendship, established and nurtured by the leaders of the two countries, has undergone all kinds of changes in the international situation.
And more lively.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and China will definitely contribute positively in building a common community of human destiny. Now look at the picture below to recall the exciting moment of China-Cambodia friendship for 63 years.
In Phnom Penh, the capital of Cambodia, there is a famous boulevard, Mao Tse Tung Boulevard. It was built on the initiative of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk in the 1960s and was funded by Chinese Premier Zhou Enlai on behalf of the Chinese people during a visit to Cambodia. Today, Mao Tse Toung Blvd is still one of the busiest streets in Phnom Penh.
On July 19, 1967, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk presented two mango trees to the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia. Today, both mango trees are branching, begging, and bearing much fruit.
On April 24, 1992, China's first Blue Hat force arrived at the port of Kampong Som in Cambodia to help repair Stung Treng Airport. From 1999 to the present, China and Cambodia have continued demining cooperation, a symbol of the inseparable friendship between the people of China and Cambodia.
In 2010, China and Cambodia established a comprehensive strategic partnership and cooperation, and in 2019, the two countries began to jointly build a common destiny community, which means that China-Cambodia strategic relations continue to develop. Grow with quality and speed.
Since 2000, China's assistance to Cambodia has reached billions of US dollars, making it Cambodia's largest donor. Most importantly, Chinese aid has never been subject to any political conditions. China has helped Cambodia build the longest roads and most bridges.
By 2020, the trade volume between the two countries will reach 9.56 billion US dollars, an increase of 1.4% in the difficult context of infectious diseases. The China-Cambodia Free Trade Agreement and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) have been signed smoothly. In May this year, Cambodia's fresh mangoes officially entered the Chinese market. Practical cooperation between China and Cambodia in various fields has continued to deepen.
