Announcing the appointment of 27 commune party officials in Bakan district, Mr. Mao Thunin instructed the recipients to work hard to serve the people and implement the law
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Provincial Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Pursat Province, on July 18, 2021, announced the decision to appoint a number of commune party officials in Bakan district. 27 people and the decision on the establishment of the Commune / Sangkat Council Election Campaign Command of the 5th Mandate 2022 at the Bakan District Party Office.
After Mr. Say Socheat, Permanent Member of Pursat Provincial Party Committee, read out the decision on the appointment of commune party office officials, then Mr. Khieu Che, Deputy Chairman of the District Party Committee and represented her as the Vice Chairman and Assistant of the Local Commune Party. Bakan as a whole has made seven commitments, including:
1: Divide the duties and responsibilities according to the Decision No. 22 of the Central Committee dated 05 September 1995 of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party on the functions, duties, structure and working mode of the Party, Provincial and District Offices. Khans and communes.
2. Organize regular meetings of district and commune party committees on a monthly basis according to the approved calendar.
3. Organize meetings with sub-commune party committees and branch committees at sub-unit offices once a month and, if necessary, hold extraordinary meetings.
4: Prepare to build programs to help the locals on a regular basis to encourage the locals and actively promote the work of the locals.
5: Prepare to strengthen the regular reporting regime to its higher party every month, if it is necessary to report orally to contact the upper level for immediate resolution.
