General knowledge: How many asteroids are there in the solar system?
(Universe): Asteroids are rocks or fragments of planets of different sizes floating in space and orbiting the sun. Do you know how many asteroids there are in the solar system?
On August 24, 2006, the General Assembly of the Federation of Global Astronomers agreed to define the term "asteroid". Large enough to have a round shape, and thirdly, there is nothing blocking the orbit. But Pluto fulfills only two principles, and its category has been downgraded to a "crumbling star."
Although it is not a definite definition, some astronomers have argued that the planets Jupiter and Neptune all have objects that block their orbits. So this is a good reason to find a solution to the reluctance of Pluto's status.
Asteroids in the innermost layers of the four solar systems are moderately large and rocky. The other four are gases, while Pluto is just one of more than 60,000 small objects resembling comets resembling objects in the Keiper region at one corner of the solar system.
