According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area also has large waterfowl, which are endangered species and some waterfowl species such as white-tailed deer, gray-tailed deer, gray snails, etc. Come down to find food in this area.
"These underscore the international importance of this protected area. Therefore, the Ministry of Environment has been preparing to put the Boeung Prek Lpou landscape protection area into a Ramsar site, which will give value to this wetland internationally. This was confirmed by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, adding that the Ministry expects the placement of the Boeung Prek Lpou landscape protection area will be done in the near future.
According to Ms. Sun Leang, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Nature Protection and Conservation Administration of the Ministry of Environment, Cambodia ratified the Ramsar Convention on December 24, 1996 and became a full member on the 23rd. October 1999. The Ramsar Convention works on three main pillars: first: the wise use of wetlands, second: the identification and creation of wetlands internationally, and third: international cooperation.
Currently, there are 2,424 wetlands designated as Ramsar sites in the world, covering an area of 25 million hectares, of which Cambodia has five sites with a total area of 42,257 hectares.
