These days, news of the panda's threat level being lowered from "endangered" to "endangered" has become a hot topic on the internet, and netizens have been actively praising and discussing it. About this "downgrade" this time. Although the panda's threat level has been lowered, conservation forces have not reduced it. The panda remains China's number one national animal.
Please note that many policies have been put in place, many plans have been implemented, as well as many fruitful results have been announced. This has led to a steady increase in the number of endangered wildlife in China, most of which have been effectively conserved and wildlife conservation work has been achieved. Notably, which has contributed to the global ecological balance.
Illegal trade is a major cause of extinction for wildlife. In 2016, the Chinese National Forestry Administration established a joint inter-ministerial conference system to combat the illegal trade in wildlife. Currently, the membership unit has been expanded from 22 initially to 27.
Conservation of wildlife and plants can not be excluded from the participation of the people. Since 2016, with the support of the National Administration of Forestry and Grasslands of China, the China Wildlife Conservation Association has organized volunteers to conduct "bird conservation operations" every year. To date, more than 3,300 activities have been carried out with the participation of more than 22,000 volunteers and more than 22,000 wild birds have been rescued.
