The draft law on e-commerce was finally approved by the National Assembly at its plenary session on October 8, 2019.
This draft law will provide important basic rules for promoting e-commerce at home and abroad with confidence through:
* Recognition of the validity, leverage, feasibility and acceptability of electronic communications, electronic records and electronic contracts *, as well as the recognition of the authenticity of electronic records and electronic signatures identified by technology and governed by state institutions. .
This draft law will actively contribute to the development of the digital economy in Cambodia, as the legal framework and legal standards that support electronic and digital activities and operations need to be developed and updated in order to build a strong digital economy. Prepare to accept the arrival of the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
In addition, the draft law will enable small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in Cambodia to integrate into the production chain and local and international markets, as well as encourage innovation and the development of new goods and services. More as well.
