Commentary: Understand the "score table" of China's foreign trade in 2021
It set a new record for the same period in history and also rose 22.8 percent from the same period before the 19 outbreak of Kovid 19 in 2019.
It should be noted that China's foreign trade data in June was stronger than most analysts had expected. China's total foreign trade volume in June reached 3.29 trillion yuan, up 22 percent from the same period in 2020, achieving growth. Positive for 13 consecutive months since June 2020.
Some foreign media outlets published articles claiming that the story was "completely unexpected." Actually, this is reasonable. Because of China's strong ability to prevent and control the spread of infectious diseases, such capabilities have provided a strong guarantee for the stability of China's basic foreign trade.
In addition, as the global vaccination framework expands and the global economy recovers, rising external demand has significantly boosted China's foreign trade. Next. More recently, international organizations have raised their forecasts for global economic growth this year. The economic recovery of countries has boosted the confidence of international trade.
China's recovery in foreign trade is not only good for itself, but also good for the world.
The internal driving force of China's foreign trade has been steadily increasing, and a number of policies and measures will continue to play a role.
