18 Fake Monks Fraudulently Walked in Kambol District Citizens Arrested
(Phnom Penh): 18 suspects disguised as monks walking to defraud people in Kambol district who were arrested by the police force of Kambol district will be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court this morning, July 15, 2021 To be punished by law.
Lieutenant Colonel Chhim Savuth, Deputy Inspector for Criminal Affairs, said that 18 suspects disguised as monks who swindled people in Phnom Penh's Kambol district were arrested by police in Prey Boeung village, Kantouk commune. Some of them are drug users.
Lt. Col. Chhim Savuth confirmed that the arrest of the 18 suspects was made on July 12, 2021 by order of Lt. Col. Hang Mony, Kambol District Police Inspector, after receiving reports from residents that A group of people came to rent a house in a New World Borey in Kambol district, and in the morning, dressed as monks, they walked around Ben Batra to raise money for local people for a long time.
On the day of the incident, 10 suspects, including nine monks and one driver, were arrested while driving a Corolla to collect fake monks from a number of targets after raising money. From local people. After questioning the suspects, the Kambol district police continued to arrest eight more suspects pretending to be monks.
After arresting the suspects as fake priests, Preah Anukun Khan Kambol decapitated them and handed over the suspects and biological evidence to the authorities for legal action. Of these suspects, seven were tested positive for drugs.
According to the confessions of the suspects, they told the authorities that they had been pretending to be monks for a long time under the auspices of the broker, Meng, who was about 25 years old. They raised 80,000 to 10,000 dong a day. Ten thousand riel, in which the broker named Meng is required to pay 30,000 to 35,000 riel per person, the rest is up to them to spend.
