At the meeting, ASEAN Foreign Ministers and US Secretary of State Anthony Blinken exchanged views on the importance of strengthening ASEAN-US relations and cooperation in economic recovery. Rehabilitation and prevention of the Kovid-19 epidemic, as well as issues of common concern and interest, both within and outside the region.
Secretary of State Anthony Blinken highlighted the role of the United States as the largest donor to the COVAX Facility and support to the region in the fight against Kovid-19 through contributions. US $ 112 million in emergency health and humanitarian assistance to ASEAN member countries.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers and the US Secretary of State also exchanged views on a number of regional and international issues that are important to regional peace, stability and security.
Regarding security and politics, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon shared concerns with other ministers on the growing complexity of the challenges posed by geopolitical competition, trade and technology, climate change and climate change. Other threats.
