Ministry of Environment calls on people to properly dispose of waste batteries and put them in public containers, supermarkets and gas stations in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment has called on people to properly dispose of waste batteries and put them in containers at a number of locations in public places, supermarkets and gas stations in Phnom Penh.
This is the appeal of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment on July 14, 2021, after the officials of the Department of Hazardous Substances Management of the Ministry of Environment put 12 batteries in public places. Supermarkets and gas stations in Phnom Penh to collect battery waste for technical management and disseminate the effects of obsolete batteries.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the preparation of battery waste bins is to manage the waste rich in hazardous substances and reduce dumping in the open or mixed with normal waste that poses a serious risk to health and the environment.
At the same time, the senior official confirmed that: "Experts of the Ministry of Environment will take the collected battery waste to be stored in the landfill, which is technically prepared for the safe management of the environment. High and learn to take advantage of those wastes.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that in order to prevent the spread of hazardous substances into the environment and protect human health from adverse effects, the Ministry of Environment is implementing a project to collect battery waste by placing 12 battery waste bins at Borey Shopping Center. Fuel includes Chip Mong Norom Mall and Chip Mong Baktouk Center, Borey Peng Huoth, Boeung Snor and PTT Petrol Stations, Wat Neak Vorn, Bokor, Phsar Touch and Boeung Snor.
The Ministry of Environment will continue to install additional battery waste bins at other locations, such as Macro Aeon Market and at some gas stations to make it easier for people to properly dispose of waste batteries and eliminate waste battery disposal. With normal waste, collect battery waste and store it properly. Experts will collect the waste batteries that people bring once a week.
According to Sophal Alaska, director of the Hazardous Substances Management Department of the Ministry of Environment, waste batteries are considered hazardous because they contain highly toxic substances such as mercury, nickel and lead.
In addition, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that Phnom Penh is the starting point for the promotion, collection and management of battery waste of the Ministry of Environment.
The Secretary of State added that after Phnom Penh, the Ministry of Environment will expand the collection of waste to three other priority provinces, including Siem Reap, Battambang and Sihanoukville and expand to other provinces.
Meanwhile, a senior official of the Ministry of Environment requested the owners of business locations, including supermarkets, gas stations and housing estates in the provinces to join the Ministry of Environment to manage and collect the waste. At the same time, people are asked to separate the waste according to the type and the battery waste, which is a dangerous waste, please store it properly and put it in the container prepared by the Ministry of Environment.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment would like to thank the site owners and residents for their cooperation and participation in the implementation of the battery waste collection project for our environment without battery waste. The Ministry of Environment calls on all citizens to continue to participate and help disseminate this battery collection project widely.
Cambodia announces Action Plan to Prevent and Respond to Child Sexual Exploitation Online 2021-2025
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 13, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, presided over the official announcement of the action plan to Prevent and respond to child sexual exploitation online 2021-2025.
Official launch of the Action Plan for the Prevention and Response of Online Sexual Exploitation of Children 2021-2025, organized by the National Council for Children in collaboration with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, the Ministry of Interior and the Committee Fight human trafficking.
To begin with, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation Vong Soth said that online sexual exploitation of children is a global problem that takes many forms and has become a new concern. Stakeholders, including the public, guardians of children, authorities and civil society, need to work together to effectively prevent and protect children from cyberbullying.
Along with these needs, children also need to receive legal justice as part of promoting the smooth and speedy recovery of child victims of sexual exploitation, both physically and mentally.
Zoe De Mealo, Country Representative of the Dutch land organization in Cambodia, said that online sexual exploitation of children is a major challenge to the protection of children around the world and in Cambodia. The use of the Internet and information technology has increased dramatically, bringing new definitions or forms of opportunities, challenges and risks to children.
She added that although most social networks do not accept profiles of children under the age of 13, many children under the age of one have a personal profile and use it on a daily basis. She states that it is estimated that about 1 million Cambodians under the age of 18 are Internet users.
On that occasion, Mr. Jala Abdel Rahab, Acting Director of UNICEF Cambodia, said that online sexual exploitation of children is a new form of child sexual abuse and exploitation facilitated by the Internet through Use of social networking sites and smartphone applications.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that this is the second time in the 6th legislature of the National Assembly that Samdech, on behalf of the Ministry of Interior, has historically participated with the Ministry of Social Affairs, Alumni and Youth Rehabilitation in the celebration and proclamation. To use the plan developed by the inter-ministerial.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stated that under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the economy and society have been further rehabilitated and developed to achieve remarkable economic growth in the last two decades and the countries in the region. And the world recognizes the rapid change of the Kingdom of Cambodia has created many more opportunities to build and develop the nation.
The fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy encourages the allocation of additional resources to education, health, social affairs and other areas, where child development is a priority in building human resources for national development and achieving sustainable development goals. Sustainability 2016-2030. This is what Prince Sar Kheng highlighted.
