(Phnom Penh): For two days, on July 12-13, 2021, the Joint Mobile Task Force for Overweight Vehicle Inspection of the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Overweight Vehicle Inspection Steering Committee launched a stop operation. 20 overweight vehicles in Siem Reap, Kandal and Kampong Speu provinces.
During the operation in Siem Reap province, in Kork Chak commune, Siem Reap city, the mobile team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport inspected 13 transport vehicles exceeding the weight limit from 5 tons to 28 tons, of which 3 vehicles Exceeding 20% of the allowable weight shall be detained for one year.
In Kandal province, on National Road No. 20, 7 transport vehicles with overweight limit from 10 tons to 22 tons were inspected.
On National Road No. 41, Kong Pisey District, Kampong Speu Province, inspected 6 transport vehicles with overweight limit from 15 tons to 20 tons, of which 4 vehicles overweight from 20% of Permissible weight is detained for 1 year.
20 overweight vehicles were fined, of which 14 vehicles were detained for one year in accordance with Article 60 of the Road Law and Notification No. 049. Proclamation on the enforcement of additional strict measures for heavy transport vehicles driving on the road network.
The Ministry of Public Works also reminded all transport company owners, truck owners and truck drivers that the Ministry will continue to strictly abide by the above laws and notices without exception.
