(Phnom Penh): Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that China is still the number one buyer of Cambodian rice and Cambodia is looking at the Chinese market and the markets of Asian countries to help ease the decline. Rice exports due to transport crisis.
Mr. Song Saran made the remarks during the "Special Guest of the Week" program entitled "Decreasing Cambodian Rice Exports to International Markets and Rehabilitation".
"Over the past six months, the Cambodian Rice Federation, as well as the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Agriculture, have tried to avoid many risks in order for us to survive rice exports," he said. "We are looking at the Chinese market. In the past six months, Cambodia has exported more than 50 percent of Cambodia's total rice exports to the Chinese market."
"The increase in rice exports to China has helped the sector a lot. If Cambodia does not have a Chinese market, there is no Asian market or there is no market of neighboring countries such as Vietnam, Cambodia," he said. "It will be very difficult in the six months from the beginning of January to June."
He added that the Rice Federation of Cambodia and the Royal Government have been very careful about the market, especially the Chinese side to increase the purchase of rice in Cambodia. On the other hand, the federation and the Royal Government have tried to help the millers to have financing to buy rice stocks and keep the reserves waiting for the market to resume shipping so that Cambodia can export normally.
He said that Cambodia is ready and still waiting for containers, so Cambodia will be able to export immediately, especially in the second quarter.
Mr. Song Saran added that it is true that in the second quarter, when the world is better, Cambodia will recover rice exports, but if these problems persist, Cambodia will still have a deficit in exports. Exit. The Cambodian Rice Federation maintains the same position: expanding the Asian and ASEAN markets to increase exports due to the long-distance market and the delivery time of 1-2 months, that is, Cambodia is very affected.
"The strategy of the Rice Federation is to continue to push for sales in the Asian market, China is still a big market where Cambodia will keep the rice stable, not the deficit, and the world will recover when the crisis of transport," he said. Delivery to the top will have a solution. "I think now there is a gradual solution, because this issue is being discussed by the big countries in the world."
Mr. Song Saran also confirmed the problem of the decline of Cambodia's rice exports that due to transportation problems hinder the export of Cambodian rice to the international market because the shipping cost increased between 5-10 times. That compares with a period without Kovid 19.
