19 Kovid Patients Give Birth Successfully at 16th January Referral Hospital in Preah Vihear Province
Preah Vihear: A woman with Kovid 19 successfully gave birth at the 16th of January Referral Hospital in Preah Vihear province on July 13, 2021 under the efforts of a team of doctors.
Dr. Kuong Lo, an adviser to the Ministry of Health and director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Health Department, said that the woman who had been infected with Kovid 19 and had given birth successfully today was Chheang Sok Heang, a 25-year-old female resident of Sra Em Cheung village. Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
Dr. Kuong Lo said that the woman was diagnosed with Kovid 19 on July 8, 2021 in Sraem market, Choam Ksan district, but she did not have any significant symptoms. No, because the woman was almost full-term pregnant, the team took her to the hospital on January 16.
Dr. Kuong Lo added that the woman had been having labor pains since yesterday and that this was her first childbirth, which caused some problems, but under the efforts of the team. Doctors also successfully delivered the baby, giving birth to a baby girl weighing 3.2 kilograms.
At the same time, Dr. Kuong Lo called on the people in Preah Vihear province to continue to be careful to protect themselves from Kovid 19, especially to continue to regularly implement the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and the guidelines of the Royal Government. To protect families and communities from Kovid.19.
