The Chinese Embassy in Cambodia announced on the morning of July 13, 2021 that the Chinese vaccines Sinofam and Sinovak have been successfully included in the list of COVAX mechanisms.
The Chinese embassy added that through this agreement, Chinese vaccines Sinofam and Sinovak will be included in the list of COVAX mechanisms that can supply the vaccine to COVAX for use in the prevention of viral diseases in developing countries from July onwards.
According to the agreement, the two Chinese companies will supply 110 million doses of Kovid vaccine to COVAX before the end of October this year and will continue to supply for a long time.
The Chinese embassy said the signing of the agreement between the two Chinese companies and the GAVI alliance was an important step in China's practical action to treat the vaccine as a "public product".
The Kovak Center is a mechanism established by a coalition of international partners, especially humanitarian organizations, in conjunction with the World Health Organization to seek vaccine supplies for poor and developing countries.
Originally, the Kovak Center used only the AstraZenica vaccine for distribution to poor and developing countries. Through the Kovak mechanism, Cambodia received 324,000 doses of the AstraZenica vaccine made in India in March.
