On July 12, 2021, Radio Free Asia reported that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, was playing the game "One bowl of water, one bowl of land" with the implementation of the national strategy to vaccinate people against Kovid 19. .
The radio station, which is considered to be a foreign reactionary radio station, considered the Royal Government of Cambodia's vaccination plan to use Chinese-made vaccines as a risky decision, so-called "one bowl of water, one bowl of land." "
The radio broadcast that "a bowl of water" is Samdech Techo will get a positive political legacy if the vaccine is used effectively. In particular, "Muy Chan Kork" will affect the Cambodian people and the reputation of the Cambodian People's Party, as well as Samdech Techo Hun Sen, if the vaccine is not effective.
The vaccine is a strategic tool for Cambodia and the world to fight Kovid 19 as well as protect the health and lives of people from the Kovid 19 pandemic. Cambodia uses two Chinese-made vaccines: Sinofam and Sinovak.
As of July 2021, Cambodia has sought 16 million doses of the vaccine, including 324,000 doses of Kovak-assisted vaccine, AstraZenica vaccine. With the advent of these vaccines, Cambodia has vaccinated nearly 5 million people.
The vast majority of Cambodians are looking forward to the vaccination and have expressed great joy after the vaccination. They are well aware of the value of vaccines in protecting their health and lives from the Kovid 19 pandemic.
RFA broadcasts have caused people on social media to express dissatisfaction and anger. They described the broadcast as "provocative and provocative" to disrupt the vaccination process, the only way to overcome Kovid 19.
"Therefore, the best option is to choose Chinese vaccines to give to our people, rather than waiting for Western vaccines to be given or sold to our government," he said. Because Kovit-19 is spreading all over the world. The old saying is that prevention is better than cure. ”
In addition to the excerpts from the comments, there are many other opinions written by Cambodians in the above RFA broadcast. Most of those comments were angry and strongly criticized and criticized the radio broadcast for this foreign policy.
Radio Free Asia, an illegal radio station in Cambodia and a tool to deceive the American public, has always broadcast the opposite of reality and against all the achievements of the Royal Government of Cambodia. His broadcast also led to criticism of Free Asia broadcasts, and some said he had never listened to the radio.
Please note that both Chinese vaccines, Sinofam and Sinofam, which are used in Cambodia are recognized by the World Health Organization and are circulating to people in no less than 100 countries in the world. In addition, the Chinese government has used both vaccines to vaccinate more than 1.3 billion people.
Many countries are now seeking vaccines, and even the World Health Organization (WHO) has expressed concern about the inequality of vaccinations in poor countries and called on countries to help provide vaccines to poor countries.
Cambodia has become one of the few countries to have vaccinated its population faster than planned. Cambodia has also become the second largest country in Southeast Asia after Singapore, which vaccinated its population quickly and in large numbers.
Not only the Cambodian people have expressed their appreciation for the plans and actions of the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on this vaccination work. Many international partners, including the World Health Organization, the World Bank and friendly countries, have also praised the fruitful results.
Thai health authorities believe that a combination of the two vaccines in such a preparation will boost immunity against Kovid 19, especially the new Delta mutation virus, which was first discovered in India.
