Speaking to Fresh News on July 12, 2021, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, said that the Ministry of Commerce believes that the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China will come into force. At the beginning of 2022.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat stated that "if Cambodia can complete the internal procedures before September 2021, the Ministry of Commerce believes that the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China will come into force in early 2022." .
In addition, the senior official of the Ministry of Commerce emphasized that the draft law on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement will be reviewed and evaluated in the upcoming plenary session of the National Assembly Standing Committee. This.
Mr. Pen Sovichet also asserted that Cambodia would further benefit from the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement on what Cambodia was receiving from the Chinese side in boosting trade volume between the two countries and Cambodia's exports.
Mr. Pen Sovichet stated that if the Cambodia-China Bilateral Free Trade Agreement enters into force, Cambodia can export more than 300 items to China without paying taxes.
According to Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, on the occasion of defending the draft law on the approval of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement with the National Assembly Expert Committee on July 08, 2021, the benefits that Cambodia received include:
1. Achieving greater and better market access for agricultural products, vegetables, fruits, processed and handicraft products, and more, while Cambodia can produce and comply with hygiene rules and standards.
2. Access to the market for trade in services that Cambodia can export in the case of skilled and qualified training, especially when Cambodia can strengthen itself in the service sector in the future.
3. Provide more investment opportunities to Cambodia, which will provide opportunities for Cambodian businessmen who wish to expand the market for services and exports to a wider range to the Chinese market.
4. Benefiting from the transfer of technology, knowledge, skills and new skills from foreign direct investment, as well as creating new jobs for the people of Cambodia, and also an important factor to strengthen the domestic production sector.
5: Clarify the procedures related to the rules of origin, customs and trade facilitation, sanitation and phytosanitary and technical barriers on trade and simplification to facilitate implementation and facilitate trade. .
6. Organizing and creating an investment and political environment to attract foreign investment.
In the five months from January to May 2021, Cambodia-China trade volume reached a total of nearly 4 billion US dollars, an increase of nearly 25% compared to the same period in 2020. This is according to the report of the Ministry of Commerce.
Cambodian goods exported to the Chinese market include: rice, chips, dried potatoes, fresh mangoes and cashew nuts and many other goods, while goods imported from China include electronics, foodstuffs, etc.
