(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Koy, General Manager of the Banking Association of Cambodia, advised the people affected by the financial crisis during the Kovid 19 Banking Association to encourage people to meet with the bank to discuss solutions. They encountered.
He said that the Banking Association is always promoting and always monitoring, and if any case occurs, the Banking Association will strive to work with members and relevant institutions to make timely solutions for the people.
According to a senior official of the Banking Association, no collateral was seized during the Kovid-19 crisis, and the Banking Association was looking for ways to ease the situation.
Heng Koy said that during the closure, the Banking Association of Cambodia played an important role in facilitating the continued provision of financial services to the public in all circumstances.
With the attention of the Royal Government and with the permission of the Guardian Authority of the National Bank of Cambodia, the Banking Association of Cambodia has been working to help banking institutions continue to provide financial services under all circumstances.
The Banking Association of Cambodia seeks to represent its members, coordinate with relevant authorities, enable employees to travel to their workplaces and ensure that banking services continue to operate.
He said that the Association of Banks in Cambodia continues to closely monitor the difficulties surrounding the concern over the repayment of loans to banks, because during the blockade, people are very difficult to travel, fear of disease and fear of the bank. Confiscated.
Please be informed that in April 2021, in order to support and facilitate customers during the difficult time of Kovid 19, the Banking Association of Cambodia and the Cambodian Microfinance Association have set out the following principles:
1: For Kovid infected patients 19: Exemption of interest payments and all penalties for 2 months and automatic credit repayment (if the client agrees) including deferment of the down payment 3 months. All customers infected with Kovid-19 must present a positive Kovid-19 test result issued by the competent authority.
2: For customers who are engaged in debt consolidation: Provides automatic loan readjustment (if the client agrees), including deferment of both principal and interest payments for 3 months and waives all penalties.
3: Continue to provide credit restructuring quickly and conveniently for clients affected by Kovid-19 disease.
4. Release emergency or supplementary loans by easing conditions and reducing interest rates to help continue and rehabilitate the family economy and business before and after the crisis.
6: Provide benefits for customers who die of Kovid-19 according to the actual possibilities of each institution.
