2. Cremation or burial of corpses that follow proper guidelines can prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus. For the safety of the organizers and transporters, those who place the body in the coffin and place the coffin on the crematorium must wear proper personal protective equipment (PPE) such as medical masks, vests and gloves. When ready, remove any used personal protective equipment and wash your hands immediately with alcohol or gel or soap and water.
3: For burial, the coffin bearer must be 4 to 6 people and must wear proper protective equipment (PPE). Family members or participants must wear protective masks properly and limit the number to no more than 10 people, and keep the distance between participants 1.5 meters apart and 3 meters away from the body. In addition, marches are not allowed.
