The Cambodian Federation of Investors Association considers the newly approved draft investment law as an important legal tool for investing in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Federation of Investors Association has announced its support for the Royal Government in its efforts to draft an investment law, with the association considering that the new draft law will be an important legal tool for further development of the investment sector in Cambodia. .
Speaking to Fresh News on July 10, 2021, Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia, said that the leadership of the Board of Directors, Executive Committee, members of the Federation of Investors of Cambodia, investors, traders, entrepreneurs, artisans. Entrepreneurs and professionals are very pleased with the Royal Government's efforts to develop this investment law.
The president of the association said that when the new law is promulgated this year or next year, it is also a good opportunity for the investment sector in Cambodia because there are many agreements that the Cambodian side is ready to make with international parties. At the same time, the context of the investment sector in Cambodia also has more and more potential under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Mr. Ley Sopheap emphasized that the Association of the Federation of Cambodian Investors is strongly committed to participating in the implementation of the content of this new investment law and to participate in promoting the development of the investment sector in Cambodia, increase good relations with international investment to contribute to the sector. National investment is growing.
Please be informed that the draft law on investment has 12 chapters and 42 articles and was approved by the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on July 9, 2021, which will be sent to the National Assembly for review and approval.
The Royal Government of Cambodia claims that the newly drafted Investment Law is to replace the old Investment Law, which came into force in 1994 and 2003.
At the same time, in order to increase the competitiveness and attractiveness of Cambodia by investors, this draft law has shortened the time to issue registration certificates from 31 days to 20 days, and the registration application can be done by submitting To use the information technology nursery (Online).
In addition, the draft law also strengthens the monitoring and control mechanism of the relevant ministries and institutions through simultaneous and joint inspections, as well as determines the incentive regime for the project. .Lc. Both tax and non-tax to attract investment flows to the sectors that Cambodia needs in the context of economic diversification and increasing competitiveness.
For the comfort of investors, this draft law incorporates some of Cambodia's international obligations to demonstrate to all investors the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect investment and provide guarantees in accordance with international law. Non-discrimination as well as investment maintenance services.
Commentary: American-style arrogance and arrogance cannot shake Hong Kong's overall stability trend
The White House announced on July 7 that it would postpone the so-called "national emergency over the situation in Hong Kong" and impose further sanctions on Hong Kong. Such an act by the United States is a serious violation of international law and the basic code of international relations, an act of hegemony that does not consider correcting its mistakes and a wrongdoing.
China has expressed outrage and condemnation. Hong Kong is a special administrative region of China, and the central government's exercise of full control over the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region is purely an internal affair of China. The White Paper on American Enterprises in China, released by the American Chamber of Commerce in China recently, shows that two-thirds of US enterprises plan to increase investment in China.
In fact, it was the US side that supported and encouraged the anti-China rebels and provoked the unrest in Hong Kong for a long time to repeatedly attack and paint China. Poses a serious threat to China's sovereignty, security and development interests!
Hong Kong's ability to raise foreign capital has also been steadily enhanced. By 2020, the volume of capital inflows into Hong Kong will reach 50,000 million US dollars, the amount of capital raised by the Hong Kong Stock Exchange for the second largest IPO in the world. A recent report by the International Monetary Fund reaffirmed Hong Kong's status as an international financial center.
Hong Kong's development depends on the hard work of Hong Kong people, on the strong support of mainland China, and never on the generosity and generosity of any foreigner. Attempts by the United States to threaten and curb Hong Kong development are not possible in the past and will not be effective now or in the future.
