Afghanistan turns to Russia, China, India for help after US full withdrawal
Kabul: The Kabul government has appealed to Russia, China and India, two neighboring countries, to help the country fight terrorism, while US troops will be completely withdrawn by the end of August. This is according to the release by Sputnik on Saturday morning, July 10, 2021.
"Peace and stability require co-operation with countries in the region and beyond to help us," Afghan National Security Adviser Hamdullah Mohib told reporters this Friday. "In the fight against terrorism without interfering in our internal affairs." Mohib added that Afghanistan always welcomes partner countries such as China, India and Russia.
So far, the United States has withdrawn more than 90 percent of its troops from Afghanistan and will be completely withdrawn before the anniversary of the September 11, 2001 terrorist attacks. But along with the Taliban, it is reported that it already occupies more than 85 percent of the territory in Afghanistan. Daily updated: As of this morning, July 10, the ASEAN region has more than 5.38 million people infected with Kovid, more than 10.3 thousand people died
The Cambodian Chamber of Commerce considers the new draft investment law, which has just been approved by the Royal Government, to attract more investment to Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, expressed his support for the new Investment Law after the draft law was approved by the Royal Government at the Plenary Meeting on July 9, 2021.
He said that on behalf of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, congratulations on the new investment law, as the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and related partners have already met twice with the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Council for the Development of Cambodia. Much to this new law.
He added that this is at a time when the head of the Royal Government is strongly committed to deepening economic reforms to keep pace with the digital industry, which is a good strategy and an additional incentive for local investors. As well as foreigners who can benefit from the new investment law.
More importantly, the new law allows the provincial investment subcommittee to approve larger projects, up from the previous $ 2 million.
Tycoon Lim Heng claims that while attending a meeting for input into the new draft investment law, the private sector has asked the provincial investment subcommittee to approve investment projects worth less than $ 10 million, which would help boost factories. Going to other provinces makes it easier for people and workers to have jobs in this place, helping to reduce poverty without having to migrate to Phnom Penh or go abroad to find work.
Please be informed that the new draft law on new investment, which has 12 chapters and 42 articles, has been approved by the plenary session of the Council of Ministers on July 9, 2021, which will be sent to the National Assembly for review and approval.
For the comfort of investors, this draft law incorporates some of Cambodia's international obligations to demonstrate to all investors the commitment of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect investment and provide guarantees in accordance with international law. Non-discrimination as well as investment maintenance services. Prey Veng continues to find 90 more Kovid 19 infected
