Tomorrow morning, another 4 million doses of vaccine will be shipped from China to Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Another 4 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine will be delivered from China to Cambodia on Saturday morning, July 10, 2021 tomorrow.
According to Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, the vaccine that will arrive tomorrow contains 3 million doses of Sinovak and 1 million doses of Sinofam. She confirmed that the 4 million doses of the vaccine was ordered by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
From February 7 to July 6, 2021, Cambodia has already received 12 million doses of vaccine. Of that, 2.2 million doses of Chinese-supplied Sinofam vaccine, 324,000 doses of Auvergne-assisted vaccine and 9.5 million doses were ordered from Cambodia.
During a special message on July 1, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in July and August 2021, Cambodia will receive 9 million doses of vaccine from China, a total of 20 million doses. Dosage according to the plan that the Royal Government seeks to give to the people.
Vaccine is a strategic tool for Cambodia to fight Kovid 19 as well as protect the health of the people from Kovid 19. Through the vaccines that Cambodia has received continuously, Cambodia can achieve its plan on vaccinating the people as well.
As of July 9, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 4.79 million people as well as foreigners in Cambodia, equivalent to more than 47.93 percent of the population vaccinated.
As a result of this vaccination work, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the Chinese government to be a strong supporter of the vaccination program.
Samdech Techo said that without Chinese support, Cambodia could not have vaccinated 200,000 people. On July 1, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced his intention to serve as a strategic reference in the supply of vaccines to Cambodia.
