(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, brought a number of materials and equipment to the bodyguard headquarters for use in disaster relief operations. Provision of materials and equipment as a consideration and preparation for the forces to intervene in case of natural disasters caused by Cambodia during this rainy season.
The handover ceremony of disaster relief equipment and equipment was held this morning, July 10, 2021, with the participation of Mr. Hang Samoeun, Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, as well as Deputy Secretary General and Advisor to the National Committee for Management. Disaster.
The ceremony was also attended by His Excellency Dr. Hing Bun Heang, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Bodyguard Command, Mr. Sous Yara, Deputy Chairman of the National Assembly Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information. Member of Parliament for Preah Vihear Province.
Lt. Gen. Ung Sarith, Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the Bodyguard Command, on behalf of General Huy Piseth and Honorary General Hing Bun Heang, recalled the direct command of General Kun Kim on the Special Intervention Forces Time for both heavy weapons during clashes along the border and participation in social security.
At the same time, during the 19-Kovid Crisis, 3,000 officers and soldiers of the Bodyguard Command launched a confrontational operation in the Red Sea area, transporting all kinds of food packages in Phnom Penh and other provinces in accordance with the order of the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Regarding disaster work, Lt. Gen. Ung Sarith said that the National Committee for Disaster Management had sent specialized officers and provided equipment to the bodyguard command to prepare for any possible disaster relief operation. Up eventually.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also continued to remind the forces to continue to adhere to the spirit of rescuing people in all emergencies, including disaster work.
"The disaster relief operation is also a battlefield," he said. This battle is also very important because we have to save the lives of the victims. "There is nothing more important than this life, so when entering this battle, we as rescuers must be determined and determined to overcome all difficulties with the utmost vigor to achieve our main goal is to save the lives of the victims."
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim also urged all officers and soldiers of the Bodyguard Command to continue to do their best work, especially the activities to help people who are suffering from the Kovid 19 problem and disaster. Other.
The Senior Minister also called on all officers and soldiers to continue to implement the measures of the Ministry of Health and the Royal Government to adhere to all the rules "3 prevent and 3 do not" to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19 to themselves, families and communities. .
