52 killed, dozens injured in Bangladesh juice factory fire
At least 52 workers have been killed in a fire at a fruit juice factory about 20 kilometers from the Bangladeshi capital Dhaka, a senior official said on Friday. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday night, July 9, 2021.
According to the authorities, a total of 18 fire units participated in the fire that engulfed the six-story building of the factory. After more than 21 hours of struggle at around 3pm, the rescue squad was able to take control.
Authorities have not yet confirmed the cause of the fire.
