(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Association of Appraisers and Real Estate Agents of Cambodia, said that although Cambodia has suffered from Kovid 19, the Cambodian real estate sector will be able to remain strong if the banking sector can continue to provide. Loans are available, while there are currently some major construction projects are still under normal development.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said this morning, July 9, 2021, during a press conference on "Real Estate and Construction in the Environment Surrounded by Kovid 19" through Zoom and with the participation Speakers: Dr. Tan Monivann, Advisor to the Cambodian Housing Development Association, Dr. Ky Sereyvath, Economist, and many journalists.
Mr. Chrek Soknim added that the real estate sector in Cambodia in 2021 is declining, but also an opportunity for investors to buy real estate, because now can be bought at a cheaper price after the situation. Used better, it will be sold at a higher price as well. He said that although Cambodia has suffered from Kovid 19, large construction projects are still developing normally.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath also said that the volume of Cambodia's international trade at the beginning of 2021 is more than in 2020, while in 2020, Cambodia faced the EBA crisis, which made consumers feel bad. The EBA pressure, and secondly, is the shortage of raw materials from China to supply the garment sector due to China's outbreak of Kovid 19.
He added that for 2021, the world has learned to live with 19 diseases, and Cambodia has also learned to live with 19 diseases, with the government reopening the economy to the people. Economic activities and living in accordance with the sanitary measures recommended by the Royal Government can only stimulate the Cambodian economy to grow again.
In the first 5 months of this year, Cambodia's exports to Thailand amounted to more than 459 million dollars!
(Phnom Penh): In the first five months of 2021, Cambodia exported more than 459 million US dollars to Thailand, down 36.61%, while imports from Thailand amounted to more than 2.905 million US dollars. . This is according to the report of the Thai Embassy in Cambodia.
The volume of bilateral trade between Cambodia and Thailand in 2020 reached 7.25 billion US dollars, down 23 percent from 9.4 billion US dollars in 2019.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has warned against the sale of rapid test equipment that the Royal Government has distributed to provinces and units.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen warned like this during the meeting of the Council of Ministers on Friday morning, July 9, 2021.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen mentioned the distribution of rapid test kits to the provinces as well as the Ministry of National Defense to be used by various units to search for Kovid 19 virus before running various programs.
Samdech Techo demonstrated the use and additional order of rapid test equipment. According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, so far, about 1 million quick test kits have been used up, and last night, about 1 million quick test kits were purchased in stock using the national budget. Samdech Techo also advised to use the funds of philanthropists to buy this quick test equipment 1 million more.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that between 4 and 5 million rapid test equipment for Cambodia has been used and purchased.
Due to the limited national budget, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also advised the ministries that can afford to buy this quick test equipment for personal use.
However, Samdech reminded the units and provinces that received this rapid test equipment should not be leaked to the market.
Please note that rapid test kits are a method that the Royal Government has authorized to be used to search for Kovid 19 virus. Currently, ministries and institutions are also using it to test participants in various programs to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
Taliban occupy key border area between Afghanistan and Iran
KABUL: Taliban insurgents on Friday said they had stormed and occupied a key area, a border crossing between Afghanistan and Iran, just hours after US President George W. Bush. Biden has issued a clear defense statement calling for the withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan. This was released by AFP on Friday evening, July 9, 2021.
An Afghan government official said efforts were being made to retake the Islam Qala, a key transit point for trade between Afghanistan and Iran. The Taliban is stepping up its offensive across the country.
The withdrawal of US troops from Afghanistan has been exacerbating the Kabul government as the Taliban escalate their offensive. Joe Biden just announced on Thursday that the United States will complete the withdrawal of troops from Afghanistan on August 31, 2021.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in an online cabinet meeting this morning, July 9, 2021, expressed concern over the spread of Kovid 19 virus on the Vietnamese border as some Vietnamese expatriates continue. Cross-border entry-exit to Cambodia.
On July 1, 2021, through that special message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen once advised to prevent the entry and exit of Vietnamese expats. However, in this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that according to the report, there are still Vietnamese people crossing into Cambodia.
In recent days, Vietnam has found 19 positive cases of Kovid, reaching more than a thousand for a few days in a row. Especially in Ho Chi Minh City, which led the authorities to take action to close the city.
Apart from Ho Chi Minh City, the provinces bordering Cambodia are also experiencing a severe Kovid 19 outbreak.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to conduct additional inspections in the provinces bordering Vietnam to stop the entry and exit of Vietnamese nationals.
For Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the entry and exit of Vietnamese people is a dangerous problem leading to the spread of Kovid 19 in the border provinces.
