The Governor of Preah Vihear Province stated that the candles and relics brought to the seven pagodas at this time were attended by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Mrs. Nhem Sakhorn and leaders. Provinces, departments, units around the province, district governors, Buddhist officials near and far.
He said that, of course, during the three months of the monks' rainy season, all the monks need lighting to study and need various relics to supply, because the rainy season is the rainy season, which makes it difficult for monks to visit. Ben Bath goes elsewhere, so candles and other relics that will be offered to monks at this time are the most necessary and bring full merit.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovann expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the two provincial priests and all pagoda management committees as well as Buddhists throughout the province who have jointly built achievements in the field of Buddhism. Notable. He also called on people to continue to protect themselves from Kovid 19 disease, to obey traffic laws, to guide children away from drugs, to be careful of natural thunderstorms this rainy season.
Please note that the 7 pagodas that received the candles and relics at this time include Wat Prasat Kork Beng, Wat Preah Puth Meanchey, Wat Po Pram Pan Deum, Wat Tuol Andet, Wat Preah Ind Trong, Wat Por Seilaram and Wat Isan Kiri Samaki Meanchey called Wat Prayuth. .
