Ms. O Vandin emphasized that "Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has decided to hand over the vaccination trucks to the provincial health departments in all 25 capitals and provinces to vaccinate the people. "More good." We would like to express our deep gratitude to Samdech Techo for his great spirit and consideration. ”
Please be informed that on July 5, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to hand over 10 vaccine trucks to the Ministry of National Defense. Cambodia earns nearly $ 6 billion from exports in 5 months 2021
(Phnom Penh): In the first five months of 2021, Cambodia exported nearly 6 billion US dollars worth of goods, an increase of 1.6% compared to the same period in 2020. This is according to the report on socio-economic trends of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The report notes that the Cambodian economy is still affected by the Kovid-19 crisis, especially the February 20 community event, which has dragged on to the present day and put pressure on key indicators of economic growth.
As of May 2021, exports of garments and garments, the number of national and international tourists, activity in the construction sector and foreign investment have been declining.
However, exports of garments and garments, such as bicycles, electronic components, wood products and other agricultural products, continued to grow well.
The report emphasizes that overall, the Cambodian economy is expected to grow positively in 2021 due to the recovery of the global economic situation and the economy of Cambodia's trading partners, the increase in demand for agricultural products and the possibility of diversion of orders and garment factories. From Myanmar to Cambodia.
