WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The administration of US President Joe Biden plans to blacklist 14 Chinese companies on economic sanctions over alleged human rights abuses in northwest China's Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region. This was released by Reuters on Friday morning, July 9, 2021.
Reuters made the report based on sources from two officials who asked not to be named. The 14 Chinese companies will be blacklisted by the US Department of Commerce on Friday (Washington time), the officials said. However, the names of the Chinese companies were not immediately available.
In June, the US Department of Commerce announced that it would blacklist five Chinese companies and entities as part of the Zhou Biden administration's efforts to get China to accept them. Responsible for US allegations that China violated human rights in Xinjiang. However, Beijing has repeatedly denied such allegations.
Kampong Siem District Authority Inspects State Boundary Adjacent to O'Svay Administration Post Fence After Allegedly Owned by Former O'Svay Post Chief
(Kampong Cham): The Joint Commission of Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, on July 08, 2021, inspected the foot of the state border post next to the fence of the O'Svay administrative post in the plan to clear any doubts to avoid conflicts. Up.
The inspection came after the media reported that two grandmothers living in a house next to the O'Svay administrative post were the land guards of Mr. Pan Don, a former O'Svay commune administrative post chief. Both live on state land, not private property.
But after the inspection, the authorities also made it clear that the two grandparents actually lived on state public land, not someone else's.
Mr. Ek Pan Don, former Chief of O'Svay Commune Administration Post, stated that during 2009 when he was the Chief of O'Svay Commune Administration Post, he met two poor people, a couple, Ta Saroeun and Yeay Say. Behind the temporary accommodation post is not owned.
Mr. Chhuon Vibol, Deputy Governor of Kampong Siem District, who led the Joint Commission force, also confirmed that his team did not have any dispute because the land has its own owner and is registered according to The system is ready and will inspect the erected structures that have been affected on the public road land? On the other hand, the whole land in O'Svay commune is already registered systematically.
