(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Red Cross Branch Committee, on July 9, 2021, accompanied by Preah Neak Mony, Provincial Chief and members of Branch Committee, invited and handed over the second house. Provincial Humanitarian Under the cooperation between the Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross and the Provincial Hall, a 31-year-old disabled man named Chek Pheak lives in Prek Tok Village, Khpob Ta Ngoun Commune, Stung Trang District.
Kampong Cham Provincial Red Cross Executive Director Touch Chhay said that Chek Pheak had a wife and two daughters. He originally had a job as a welder, but unfortunately two years ago, while welding the roof of his house, he was electrocuted, causing both of his legs to rot and eventually to be amputated below the knee, leaving him paralyzed and unable to work. .
Mr. Touch Chhay said that the family, in addition to the state support through a poor card, the head of the family fell on his sister, who was a housewife, forced to work as a weeder or seasonal farm for a living. Raising day for a disabled husband and two daughters. With limited resources, the family lives in dilapidated huts covered with old galvanized iron provided by their neighbors.
Seeing this difficult situation, Mr. Un Chanda decided to provide a wooden house high above the zinc roof (size 4m × 6m) for the family to stay, which will cost almost all the construction cost. 10 million riels, of which the provincial Red Cross branch contributed 1 million riels and Mr. Un Chanda donated 1 million riels, the provincial chief 1 million riels. In addition, it is the additional contribution of philanthropists and the mobilization team and fund management of the program.
Separately, 13 other needy families who participated at that time received gifts in each family, including rice, fish, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce and T-shirt, as well as a budget of 20,000 riels.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on July 9, 2021 issued a press release confirming the resumption of 988 new Kovid cases with 988 cases while 897 patients were cured.
Please be informed that as of the morning of July 9, 2021, Cambodia has found a total of 59,045 19 cases of Kovid, of which a total of 50,917 have been cured and a total of 855 have died. Draft Law on Investment has been fully approved by the Royal Government
(Phnom Penh): The draft law on investment was fully approved by the Royal Government in the meeting of the Council of Ministers led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia this morning, July 9, 2021.
Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, emphasized that the draft law is an amendment to the wording and content of Article 9, Chapter 3.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said at the meeting that the proposed law is a legal basis to attract and provide easy scope for investors to invest in Cambodia.
Please note that the Draft Law on Investment is a new draft law that was initiated and indicated by the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy Document 2015-2025.
Mr. Phay Siphan confirmed that the study and drafting of this preliminary law was carried out strictly by the Council for the Development of Cambodia (FCDC). In the process of drafting the law, several meetings were held with private sector representatives and other stakeholders to collect input.
The Deputy Prime Minister added that the draft law on investment is designed to create an open, transparent and predictable legal framework that is favorable for investment to attract and promote investment. Invested by Cambodian or foreign individuals with quality, efficiency and effectiveness to develop the socio-economic situation in Cambodia.
The draft law is also designed to be flexible, with special incentives for specific sectors and investment activities that have high potential to contribute to national development in line with government policies. This particular will be set out in the Financial Law for Management.
To provide investors with warmth, the draft law incorporates some of Cambodia's international obligations to demonstrate to all investors the Royal Government of Cambodia's commitment to protect investment and provide guarantees in accordance with international law. Non-discrimination as well as investment maintenance services.
In the context of the crisis of Kovi 219, which is plaguing the world, including Cambodia, this draft investment law is very important for Cambodia, as it will make Cambodia more attractive for foreign direct investment. And domestic investment.
