BEIJING: Although some Western Chinese opposition groups have repeatedly attacked and painted China, the effectiveness of Hong Kong's implementation of national security laws over the past year has confirmed that This not only protected the security, national sovereignty and development interests of China, but also the interests and well-being of the people of Hong Kong.
The American Chamber of Commerce in Hong Kong conducted a referendum that showed that 77 percent of the respondents noted that living conditions in Hong Kong were better. The number of foreign media and journalists going to work in Hong Kong is also increasing.
Currently, about 9,000 Chinese and foreign enterprises have set up offices in Hong Kong, of which more than 40% are regional headquarters.
* Third: Hong Kong has a promising future. This year, China launched the 14th Five-Year National Development Plan, which will bring new opportunities to Hong Kong's development. Hong Kong's national security law has undoubtedly brought about a safe and stable environment, which has created favorable conditions for Hong Kong to better integrate with the general situation of national development.
In the first quarter of this year, Hong Kong residents' total income rose 7.5 percent year-on-year, according to data released by the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. Each of the previous years. Wealth per capita ranks third in the world. In addition, Hong Kong's GDP in the first quarter of this year increased by 7.9% compared to the same period last year, the economy began to recover.
