"The US military mission in Afghanistan will end on August 31. The people of Afghanistan have the right and responsibility to determine their own destiny," Biden said.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - US President Joe Biden on Thursday announced that the US military mission in Afghanistan will end on August 31 for nearly 20 years. After it started. This was released by AFP on Friday morning, July 9, 2021.
"The United States will not be able to continue to adhere to policies designed to respond to the global situation as it did 20 years ago," Biden said. We need to respond to the threats that are happening today. The United States did not go to Afghanistan to build that country. "Now it is the right and responsibility of the Afghan people alone to decide their future."
