Samdech Techo Hun Sen Celebrates the Royal "Tree Day" Ceremony and Calls for the Protection and Planting of Trees
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, celebrates the Royal "Tree Day" which Cambodia always celebrates every year on July 9.
With the celebration of the Royal "Tree Day", Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, called on the Cambodian people to take care of the forest and plant seedlings for the benefit of the environment and living.
Samdech Techo highlighted on his Facebook page, "Let the Cambodian people all over the country love and protect the forest and plant seedlings to protect the natural environment everywhere for the benefit of our community." "We and all kinds of wildlife, as well as biodiversity, are the property of humankind in every generation."
Samdech Techo thanked the relevant ministries, departments, authorities and authorities at all levels, as well as associations of national and international organizations, donors and development partners, as well as the people who participated in maintaining, protecting and planting more trees throughout the country.
Please be informed that the Royal "Tree Day" was established in 1952 under the leadership of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk in order to inspire the movement to replant trees and preserve forest resources. Especially to preserve, protect and cultivate love for the forest and the natural environment.
This royal ceremony is held every year on July 9, choosing a location to plant seedlings under the presidency of the King of Cambodia, but for the last two years, the royal ceremony has not been organized. Due to the outbreak of Kovid 19.
