(Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has stressed that peace and stability are a priority for foreign investment in Cambodia, despite global political and trade challenges.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized this in the meeting of the Council of Ministers held online this morning, July 9, 2021.
At the meeting, which discussed the draft law on investment, Samdech Techo highlighted that the proposed law is a legal basis for attracting and providing scope for investors to invest in Cambodia. This is according to Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, who quoted Samdech Techo's speech and shared it on social media.
Mr. Phay Siphan quoted Samdech Techo as saying, "Investors need peace and stability, which is a priority in deciding to take Cambodia as an investment destination, regardless of the international situation in the political and trade situation."
According to the report of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC), in the first half of 2021, the Cambodian Investment Committee and the Cambodian Special Economic Zone Committee approved the investment of 87 new projects and production expansion projects with capital. The total investment is nearly 3 billion US dollars, creating 50,029 jobs.
Compared to the same period in 2020, this investment project has decreased by about 63 projects. However, investment capital did not decrease, but increased by about 12 percent due to some large investment projects with high investment.
China is the largest investor in Cambodia in the first half of 2021. Chinese companies have invested more than 2 billion US dollars.
It should be noted that in the Cabinet meeting chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, the draft law on investment was discussed.
The Draft Law on Investment is a new draft law that was initiated and indicated by the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy Document 2015-2025.
Mr. Phay Siphan confirmed that the study and drafting of the preliminary draft law was carried out strictly by the Council for the Development of Cambodia (FCDC). In the process of drafting the law, several meetings were held with private sector representatives and other stakeholders to collect input.
