The following is the press release of Kampong Thom Provincial Administration: Kampong Chhnang provincial authorities have solved the case of killing a man who is the leader of a contemporary band.
(Kampong Chhnang): Police in Kampong Chhnang province have separated the case of a man who is the leader of a contemporary band who has been missing for more than 10 days on July 8, 2021, after conducting a search operation for missing persons for a long time. More than 10 days. In this case, the authorities have not yet identified the perpetrator.
It should be reminded that a man known as the leader of the contemporary band named Chan Kien, over 50 years old, living in Utumpor village, Svay Chrum commune, Rolea Bier district, disappeared on the night of June 27, 2021 while the victim was driving his own car. Black Tacoma with license plate Kampong Chhnang 2A. 2626 came to Kampong Chhnang province and disappeared forever.
After the disappearance, the family and members of the contemporary band complained and reported to the authorities to search for the victim.
Under the efforts of the provincial police, under the direction of Major General Khov Ly, the provincial police commissioner and with the coordination of the prosecutor of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, the police found the victim's car in Phnom Penh.
However, due to the operation and research, the police did not disclose this information yet, only on the afternoon of July 8, the police separated the case and arrested the perpetrators to interrogate and build a case. The suspect has not been identified yet, is being questioned and the suspect's answer is still unclear.
According to a source from the police, who asked not to be named, during the search operation, the police arrested two people who bought a car from the suspect who said it was a duty-free car. Got one.
The source added that the suspect confessed that the victim's body was dumped at the Prek Samrong Bridge in Takhmao City, Kandal Province. As for the cause of the murder, the authorities will confirm tomorrow.
Stung Treng Province Receives Humanitarian Assistance from Plan International for Use in Combating Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The Stung Treng Provincial Administration has received humanitarian assistance from Plan International in Stung Treng Province for use in the fight against Kovid 19 in the province.
The handover took place in the presence of Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province, with the participation of Mr. Phen Bun Phoeun, Executive Director of Stung Treng Program of Plan International, Deputy Director of Health Department of Provincial Administration and some stakeholders this morning. This is July 8, 2021.
Mr. Phen Bun Phoeun said that the delivery of humanitarian aid by Plan International in Stung Treng came after seeing the shortage and increase of 19 cases of Kovid in 19 provinces.
He said that the humanitarian assistance provided to the provincial administration is in line with the operations of Plan International, which has always contributed to the Royal Government in humanitarian and social affairs.
Mr. Mom Saroeun thanked Plan International in Stung Treng for providing material assistance and participating in humanitarian activities with the provincial administration now and in the past, which have contributed significantly to the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19. As well as alleviating some of the shortcomings of the provincial administration and helped alleviate the hardships of the people.
Mr. Mom Saroeun continued that all the humanitarian aid that Plan International and various charities have supported the provincial administration will be used for the right purpose without causing any concern or disappointment to the philanthropist.
At the same time, the Governor of Stung Treng Province also handed over the materials donated by Plan International in Stung Treng Province to the Provincial Health Department of the Provincial Administration to be used at the target of Chattalysak Level 2, where 19 Kovid patients are resting. Treat well.
It should be noted that the humanitarian aid provided by Plan International to the Stung Treng Provincial Administration now includes 300 beds for patients, 300 liters of alcohol, 3,500 masks, 5,000 pairs of medical gloves and 300 cases of purification.
Minister of Commerce Defends Draft Law on Approval of Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement with National Assembly Expert Committee
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 08, 2021, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led an inter-ministerial delegation to defend the draft law on the ratification of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement with an expert committee. Of the Assembly conducted via video system.
On that occasion, the Minister of Commerce informed Ms. Nin Saphon, Chairperson of the Ninth Committee of the National Assembly and members, about some of the major benefits that Cambodia has received from the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China. According to the Minister, the benefits that Cambodia receives include:
Especially in the context of the Kovid-19 epidemic crisis, this agreement will also help the strategy to rehabilitate the Cambodian economy, which has been severely affected by Kovid-19, as well as help normalize socio-economic stability. New Cambodian society through the growth of exports to the Chinese market and the flow of investment into Cambodia, which will help create jobs and income for people.
After listening to the interpretation and explanation to Ms. Nin Saphon and members of the Ninth Committee of the National Assembly, they fully supported the draft law on the approval of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement and expressed their appreciation to the negotiating team that led it. By the Minister of Commerce, who worked hard to successfully complete the negotiations in accordance with the mandate provided by the head of the Royal Government.
