Check out the pictures! Celebrating the 4th Anniversary of the Inclusion of Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List
(Phnom Penh): Sambor Prei Kuk temple is located in Sambo village, Sambo commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province, about 30 km north of Stung Sen city. The area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple is large and there are 7 villages in that area. Sambor Prei Kuk is divided into two major areas: the former capital area on the west side and the temple area on the eastern side, separated by a stream called Kru Ke.
Sambor Prei Kuk is the former capital of Isanpura of the Chenla Empire between the late 6th and early 7th centuries AD, the work of King Isanvarman I. The temple is built of ancient bricks, inscriptions, water retainers, city walls and other shrines.
On July 08, 2021, this is the fourth anniversary of this ancient Khmer temple being inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List. To know more about Sambor Prei Kuk, please visit the picture below:
