This morning, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, expressed his congratulations on this happy day of the Cambodian nation. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted that the inclusion of these cultural treasures and ancient temples in the World Heritage List not only received international protection, but also helped promote Cambodian cultural treasures and ancient temples to the international stage. Also.
Samdech Techo added, "After being registered as a World Heritage Site, Sambor Prei Kuk Temple has become an attractive cultural and historical tourist site."
The Prime Minister also continued to call on the Cambodian people to take part in preserving all the ancient temples throughout the country for the benefit of all generations of Cambodians.
Please be reminded that Sambor Prei Kuk was inscribed on the World Heritage List at the 41st Summit of the World Heritage Committee, which was held on July 2-12, 2017, with 193 member countries and 21 countries. As a standing committee.
The inclusion of Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List is a great achievement for the mission to protect the ancient temples and to promote the cultural heritage of the Khmer people left by their ancestors. To celebrate the historic day of achievement in the protection of Khmer cultural heritage in this era of peace, the Royal Government has decided to designate July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance Day as a World Heritage Site. .
Despite the relocation of the capital to Angkor in the 9th century, the Sambor Prei Kuk area remained an important religious center during the Angkorian period, with additional religious structures and the restoration of existing structures for subsequent worship. The Sambor Prei Kuk temple resort has been built for many generations, highlighting the temples, statues and other works of art and has become a famous historical site in Cambodia today.
