(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, chaired a meeting to review and strengthen the implementation of the project of construction of rainwater and sewage system in Stung Sen City on July 7, 2021 at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
Mr. Sok Loo thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, for providing a project to build a sewer system and wastewater treatment plant in Kampong Thom province. The project is a government project, a loan from the Asian Development Bank (ADB), with a total budget of more than $ 12 million, including more than 22 km of drainage and many other infrastructure.
The provincial governor requested the construction company to speed up the construction because if there is no drainage system, Stung Sen city will be flooded due to rain.
Mr. Sok Lou also warned the officials to inspect all the constructions that have been built, especially the pouring of soil, the construction of houses, the construction of fences, etc., which have violated the road, pouring soil higher than the road will make There is congestion without drainage system, water system and optical cable.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Lou called on the people to participate in the construction, because the construction process of the drainage system to release rain or dirty water is done on the food in front of the people's houses. Resolving the impact Only with the participation of the people can the construction company speed up its process smoothly.
The Governor of Kampong Thom Province underlined that "In order for all this work to be more effective, all citizens should continue to respect the law by asking the relevant authorities, especially all commune chiefs, to help educate the people to have a high sense of responsibility. "Maintain the drainage system and store waste properly in homes, public places and so on."
Mr. Chou Kolla, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Thom Province, said that the implementation of the project to build a system to release rainwater, wastewater and treatment tanks in Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province, including:
First, the construction of a wastewater treatment plant with a filtration capacity of about 2,500 cubic meters per day, the construction of a 39.2-kilometer-long sewer and a 17.1-kilometer-long sewer network.
Second, the construction of a landfill with a storage capacity of 48,000 cubic meters and the installation of garbage collection vehicles and waste storage.
He said that the construction project will last for three years, implemented from July 2020 to July 2023.
