BEIJING, July 6 (Xinhua) - Xi Jinping, secretary-general of the CPC Central Committee and chairman of the National People's Congress (NPC), said at a meeting between the leaders of the Communist Party of China (CPC) and the world's political parties that China will actively promote Strengthening global governance to make a new contribution to human handshake in tackling common challenges.
Xi Jinping said that international law must be accepted by all countries around the world, but not by minorities. Cooperation between nations should be regarded as the object of service to humanity as a whole, but not to the pursuit of global domination by a handful of political groups.
The parties must unite against hegemony and strong power politics. He reiterated that China is one of the great families of developing countries and will make unremitting efforts to promote the representation and freedom of expression of developing countries in the international governance system.
Xi Jinping emphasized that the path to modernization has no absolute formula, and that the right formula for development is the best. Each country's efforts to find a path to modernization appropriate to its own situation should be commended.
