(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of the 13th anniversary of the designation of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site on July 7, 2021, Mr. Phay Siphan, Head of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government of Cambodia, issued a message reminding that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director The Cambodian Minister at the time did not rest overnight to monitor the results of the 2008 Preah Vihear World Heritage Site trial.
Mr. Phay Siphan said: "In this, I still remember that Samdech Techo did not rest all night watching the decision of the committee in Quebec City, Canada. "We remember that in pagodas, state institutions and schools, there was a gathering of monks, government officials and students to play drums and bells at 7 am to celebrate the Temple of Preah Vihear has been inscribed on the World Heritage List."
"With this, we would like to pay tribute to the late Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An with his experience as a lesson and a history of great success for this nation," he said.
Please be informed that on November 11, 2013, the Hague Court of Justice upheld the 1962 decision filed by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, stating that the Temple of Preah Vihear belongs to Cambodia.
