The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts issued a press release regarding the construction of a stone temple in Borei Rom Province, Thailand, similar to Angkor Wat (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts issued a press release on July 7, 2021. And the construction of a stone temple in Borei Rom province of Thailand, similar to Angkor Wat.
In the past few days, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has been in close contact and cooperation with the Embassy of the Kingdom of Cambodia in the Kingdom of Thailand in connection with the construction of a stone temple in Borei Rom Province, Thailand. Research to gather more information.
The Embassy of the Kingdom of Cambodia has carefully researched and collected some preliminary information as follows:
1. The construction of this temple is one of the other stone temple structures, which is a combination of the place of worship of the Buddha image, located in Wat Puthbat Seila Phumanfa, Nong Bo Lay Village, Ban Sing Commune, Nang Rang District, Borei Rom Province, Kingdom of Thailand. . The construction is made of sandstone on the outside and cast concrete embedded in steel from the inside.
2: By clarifying and showing the documents of the construction plan, the abbot of the pagoda confirmed that the construction of this temple did not copy the design or build in the same architectural style as the temple of Angkor Wat or any ancient temple in Cambodia. It is built according to the layout itself and designed according to the architecture of some of the temples in the area.
3. The representative of the coordinator of the temple construction project also welcomes the request to request a professional officer in the field of Cambodian architecture to visit directly in case of doubt.
The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts would like to express its deep gratitude to our compatriots who have always taken care to protect and enhance the prestige, national identity as well as the noble art and culture of the nation with high dignity. The Ministry will work and monitor this work closely.
Mrs. Try Dana and Tycoon Hing Panharith donated $ 35,000 to the Cambodian Red Cross to help build houses for poor Cambodian veterans in Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Try Dana, CEO of Dana Tri (Cambodia) Trading Co., Ltd. and Tycoon Hing Panharith donated $ 35,000 to the Cambodian Red Cross to help build houses for poor Cambodian veterans in Phnom Kravanh District, Pursat Province.
The handover ceremony took place at the headquarters of the Cambodian Red Cross on July 7, 2021, presided over by Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross with Ms. Try Dana, General Director of Dana Tri (Cambodia) Trading Company. Co., Ltd. and Duke Hing Panharith.
On that occasion, the First Deputy Secretary General warmly welcomed and conveyed the words of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who paid a courtesy call and expressed his deep gratitude for the generosity of Ms. Try Dana. And Tycoon Hing Panharith, who donated money to the Cambodian Red Cross.
In addition, the First Deputy Secretary General informed that the Cambodian Red Cross provided through the Cambodian Veterans Association $ 500,000 as the first step on February 8, 2021 and 1 million dollars. The second step on July 6, 2021.
The Cambodian Red Cross has already handed over 50 houses as the first step to 50 families of poor Cambodian veterans on June 12, 2021, and is scheduled to hand over 130 houses - 150. The back is the second step in the coming August 2021.
In response, Ms. Try Dana and Duke Hing Panharith thanked Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for allowing them to contribute to humanitarian work with the Cambodian Red Cross, a national association that has always been active in humanitarian activities to help the people. Extremely vulnerable and has built trust from philanthropists from all walks of life.
