(Phnom Penh): July 7 marks the 13th anniversary of the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site at the 32nd Meeting of the UNESCO World Heritage Committee on July 7. 2008 in Quebec City, Canada.
Please watch the documentary video prepared by the National Authority of Preah Vihear. Daily updated: As of this morning, July 7, the ASEAN region has more than 5.19 million people infected with Kovid, more than 9,960,000 people died.
Through the Facebook page of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia joined in celebrating the day when the Temple of Preah Vihear was declared a World Heritage Site.
Samdech Techo considers the event of placing the Temple of Preah Vihear on the World Heritage List as a new historical event since Cambodia received this sacred temple after winning the case against Thailand at the International Court of Justice in The Hague on June 15. 1962
With congratulations, Samdech Techo also called on the Cambodian people to work together to preserve all the ancient temples of Cambodia to survive as a legacy for the next generation of Cambodians.
Preah Vihear Temple is a sacred temple of Cambodia located on Dangrek Mountain, 625 meters above sea level in Sraem Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, about 100 km north of Preah Vihear City and about 230 km northeast of Siem Reap City and About 414 km north of Phnom Penh.
Please be reminded that in the cause of upholding the national cultural heritage and defending national sovereignty, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, sent a letter to UNESCO in 2001 requesting the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site. The Prime Minister said that the inscription of the Temple of Preah Vihear on the World Heritage List is in line with the planned plan, which is a priority of Cambodia's foreign policy.
To celebrate this great achievement, the Royal Government of Cambodia has designated July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance for the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List and recommended the celebration. Also celebrated. Do not drive at the speed limit! 3 killed and 2 injured in traffic accidents nationwide on July 6 yesterday
