Pursat Governor Develops Livestock and Animal Husbandry Competition for Veterans
"Bun Rany Sen Chey Damnak Troyeung" village is a newly established village organized by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for veterans in Pursat province. This village covers an area of more than 900 hectares, which is a social land concession provided by the Royal Government to 628 families of veterans in Pursat province. Each family receives 70 x 150 meters of land for housing and cultivation.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who was named the Mother of Humanity after the support of various philanthropists, also helped to build houses for the 628 families of the veterans. In addition, the Royal Government, headed by Samdech Techo, also planned to build schools, health centers, water wells, roads and electricity to this village.
The Cambodian Veterans Association, with Senior Minister Kun Kim as Secretary-General and Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal staff, has been actively and actively promoting this event. Mr. Mao Thunin, the direct operator of this work, paid the highest attention, although he was busy with the necessary work in the province, however, he always went to inspect the construction of this village directly.
About 128 houses for veterans have been built and 50 houses were handed over to veterans on June 12, 2021. Many families of veterans have come to live in their homes and lands, the happiest places in their lives.
Mr. Mao Thunin has been focusing on the construction of houses, clearing land, planting crops, as well as building infrastructure. Mr. Mao Thunin also took care of the living and building of the lives of the veterans who came to live there. Mao Thunin organizes monthly food donations to the families of veterans who come to live in the area.
This past Sunday, the provincial governor brought some food donations to distribute to the families of 150 veterans living there. Each family receives 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles and 1 can of soy sauce or fish sauce. The offer is for a full year to ensure that the families of the veterans do not face a lack of livelihood while they are busy preparing their homes and growing crops.
During the distribution ceremony, Mr. Mao Thunin also announced the establishment of a competition program in growing vegetables, crops and raising animals for the families of veterans in the village to promote the construction of a better life for veterans.
According to Mr. Mao Thunin, the competition program will be summarized at the end of the month by determining the winners from 1st to 5th place by giving points on cultivation, animal husbandry and housekeeping. To support the veterans' market for vegetables and animals, Mao Thunin also plans to set up a place to buy vegetables and animals that can be grown and raised.
In front of the families of the veterans at that time, Mr. Mao Thunin also reminded of the attention of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as Senior Minister Kun Kim, who always urged him to come and check. On living and building houses as well as infrastructure.
Mr. Mao Thunin also advised all the families of veterans to know how to love and take care of the house, which is a great gift of Samdech Kittiprittbandit, and this house and land should not be sold as an inheritance for future generations. Preah Vihear Provincial Public Works Department Leaders and Officials Delive Over 20 Million Riels to the Cambodian Red Cross Branch
