(Phnom Penh): The Swedish government has officially requested the Royal Government of Cambodia to open an honorary consulate in Phnom Penh. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, obtained by Fresh News.
"The Ambassador agreed that Cambodia and Sweden have a long and special relationship from the current difficult situation to the present," the Foreign Ministry said. In particular, Sweden has officially requested the opening of an honorary consulate in Phnom Penh.
On November 26, 2020, the Swedish Embassy in Cambodia announced the closure of its Embassy in Phnom Penh at the end of 2021. The embassy claimed that Sweden has always had good relations with Cambodia and will continue to do so through other means after the embassy closes. However, Cambodia does not have its own embassy in Sweden.
