(Phnom Penh): Children's Kitchen Organization on July 4 continued to distribute food to more than 100 needy people in Phnom Penh. Today's food distribution took place at the Children's Kitchen on the grounds of Chey Chumneas Primary School.
Children's Kitchen is a food depot that is always doing humanitarian work, sharing food to the general poor. The organization receives support from philanthropists and its main goal is to share food with the needy and provide daily food to orphans and scavengers, as well as train them to be good people in society. .
The president of Children's Kitchen said that in this organization, the volunteers are all children and young people who used to be scavengers and the needy. Now some of the volunteers in the organization go to general school and have enough knowledge to do charity work, and some, even at a young age, can speak a foreign language and seek help.
The president of the Children's Kitchen said that before the 19th Kovid outbreak, the organization used to feed 200 to 300 children every day, but the organization had no place to live. In addition, the organization always plans to distribute food to the poor in various locations in Phnom Penh and some provinces.
From its inception on February 1, 2011 to July 2, 2021, Children's Kitchen has provided food to many orphans and malnourished people, contributing to the government's efforts to reduce poverty. .
