Mr. Tep Horn, Chairman of Maung Russey District Sub-Committee, stated that on the afternoon of June 28-29, 2021, Maung Russey District was hit by two strong winds, affecting 5 communes in 13 villages in That affected a total of 173 houses, 13 severely affected houses, 76 moderately affected houses and 84 lightly injured houses, 2 schools, 2 festivals, as well as damaged some equipment.
Although the small amount of humanitarian donations brought to you today is not enough for the loss of the family, it can also provide some relief and also an expression of concern for Every citizen by the special leadership, the Cambodian Red Cross, as the slogan "I and the Cambodian Red Cross do not leave anyone."
Materials to be provided to each family to receive donations include: 25 kg of rice, 1 bottle of pure water, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of sarong, 1 scarf, 1 mosquito net, 1 blanket, 1 bottle of alcohol, 10 masks and some money.
