TOP NEWS: Royal Government of Cambodia decides to pay tuition fees to 6 Cambodian military students who were cut off by US for political reasons
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on July 2, 2021 decided to continue to pay tuition fees until the end for the six Cambodian military academy students who were cut off by the United States for political reasons. This is according to the announcement of the spokesman of the Ministry of National Defense, which was received by Fresh News.
A spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of Defense considered the scholarship cut for six Cambodian students to be a unilateral decision by the United States. At the same time, the Ministry has prepared urgent and necessary action related to the study of six Cambodian military academy students who are studying in US military academies.
It should be noted that six Cambodian students who are studying through scholarships at four military academies in the United States have been told to suspend their studies before the deadline. All six students are studying at West Point Military Academy. Two academies, two airmen, one navy and one coast guard.
The decision to suspend the scholarship has drawn strong criticism of the United States for making immoral decisions for political reasons, as the two countries have been at loggerheads in the past.
