The relics and candles of Preah Vossa of Oknha Prit Moha Upasika Thomman Vivathana Bun Seangly were donated to 8 pagodas in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province
(Phnom Penh): The relics and candles of Preah Vossa of Duke Prith Moha Upasika Dhammanhan Vivathana Bun Seangly, the mother-in-law of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the mother-in-law of Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen were given to the monks at the pagoda 8 in Phnom Penh and Kandal Province on the occasion of Vesak Day.
Fortune-telling objects and candles were given to monks on the morning of Friday, July 2, 2021. Mrs. Bun Sotha invited representatives of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to bring the relics and candles of Preah Vossa to the eight pagodas.
Vesa festival is always held every year from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch. The ceremony started on the evening of the 15th day of the month of Asat, with the participation of the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda, the procession of candles, skirts and other paraphernalia, the procession around the temple, and then the performance of sermons and the offering of candles. Monks.
