India sets up "advanced experts" and sends them to states to increase Kovid-19 prevention
NEW DELHI: The Federal Government of India on Friday began sending high-level teams to states with increasing cases of COVID-19 infection in order to improve the rapid response system to outbreaks. This was released by Xinhua on Friday afternoon, July 2, 2021.
According to the New Delhi government, the task force is tasked with identifying key issues in the states most vulnerable to the COVID-19 pandemic. Understanding the real problems and origins of this infection will enable all professional groups to provide advice so that all state authorities can act more quickly and effectively.
The task force includes the medical and public health teams, which are tasked with conducting immediate inspections of COVID-19 outbreaks in the reported areas. According to the Indian Ministry of Health, they are also in charge of analyzing and calculating the need for medical equipment in areas where COVID-19 infection is occurring.
