(Phnom Penh): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Immunization Commission, said that more than 400 people between the ages of 90 and 103 have been vaccinated and have no health problems. .
As a public health expert, O Vandin encourages all older people to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 because the elderly are at greater risk of Kovid 19 attacks.
A statement encouraging the elderly to get vaccinated came as Mrs. O Vandin handed over a gift from Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen to a 101-year-old woman who volunteered to be vaccinated in China this morning. This is July 2, 2021.
Mrs. Ho Kham is a resident of Phnom Penh. She is an elderly person who has learned about the value of vaccines and has volunteered to be vaccinated against Kovid 19.
According to her son, she came to get vaccinated from her own heart, without any encouragement from her children.
Ho Kham already vaccinated the first dose of Sino-Vaccine on the morning of July 2, in front of reporters' cameras. According to the son, the grandmother who likes to eat only fruits and vegetables is healthy and after the vaccination is not harmful to his health.
Ms. O Vandin considered Ho Kham's visit to be vaccinated as a model for other elderly people and also confirmed the safety of vaccines for the elderly.
"The current vaccination for her is to show the public that it is very important, even though she is 101 years old, but the vaccine still has important benefits. "Protect the lives of people." This is the confirmation of Mrs. O Vandin.
On that occasion, Ms. Ou Vandin also pointed out that the elderly are a group of people who are at risk of severe attacks from Kovid 19, which requires vaccination to fight the disease. She encouraged all older people to get vaccinated.
"Let the family help explain and give them confidence and warmth so that they can make the right decision in getting the Kovid 19 vaccine," said Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. "He tried to buy this vaccine to give to our people."
It should be noted that as of July 1, Cambodia vaccinated more than 4.3 million people living and working in Cambodia, equivalent to more than 43% of the population of about 10 million vaccinated. .
Ms. O Vandin confirmed that the vaccination may be completed as planned by November 2021.
More than 4.3 million people who have been vaccinated have no information about the health risks of the vaccine. Nowadays, Cambodians are becoming more aware of the benefits of vaccines, and getting vaccinated is one of their strong desires.
