Ministry of Tourism Holds National Workshop on Rehabilitation of Cambodia Tourism in and After Kovid-19 Crisis
The purpose of the workshop was to exchange experiences and information from all stakeholders on the tourism rehabilitation plan, the direction of organizations and institutions to change the challenges caused by Kovid-19 to become opportunities in tourism, especially to promote Implementation of the roadmap on tourism rehabilitation during and after the Kovid-19 crisis of 2021-2025 submitted by the Royal Government.
Mr. Thong Rathsak said that the workshop was to share the plan to restore tourism in and after the Kovid 19 crisis to the public, the private sector, all partners and stakeholders to participate in the implementation for 2021-2025. It is especially good to get new entrances in addition to entrepreneurship development, technology promotion in tourism and the concept of the tourism industry association in post-crisis tourism recovery.
Mr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurship, expressed his support for entrepreneurship in the tourism sector through recent cooperation with the tourism sector, focusing on the promotion of tourism entrepreneurship in the coastal region, as well as training plans. Tourism into the community as well.
Please note that the workshop was divided into two main topics:
* First, the plan to rehabilitate tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis, with guest speakers from the Ministry of Tourism, CEO of Khmer Entrepreneurship, CEO of One De Pass, former CEO of Mekong Tourism Coordination Office and President of the Cambodian Tourism Federation.
2: Promoting digital technology for quick payment in the tourism sector in Cambodia with the participation of representatives from the private sector, the Tourism Industry Association and representatives of the Cambodian Center 4.0.
